    <node id="823afe12-1e56-45a2-b980-e7b0be0c2fc2">
      <data key="d0">{"name":"Life Insurance Policy Features","text":"───────────────────────────────────┐\n│  SECTION 4: DEATH BENEFIT OPTIONS                                 │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n4.1 OPTION I - Level Death Benefit\n    Death Benefit = Face Amount\n    Lower charges but no growth from investments\n\n4.2 OPTION II - Variable Death Benefit (CURRENTLY SELECTED)\n    Death Benefit = Face Amount + Account Value\n    Higher charges but death benefit grows with account\n\n4.3 You may switch between options subject to:\n    • Proof of insurability for increases\n    • Minimum face amount requirements\n    • $50 administrative fee\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  SECTION 5: INVESTMENT RISK DISCLOSURE                            │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n5.1 IMPORTANT: The account value and death benefit (under Option II) \n    are NOT guaranteed and will fluctuate based on sub-account \n    performance.\n\n5.2 Investment risk is borne entirely by the policy owner.\n\n5.3 Poor investment performance can cause the policy to lapse if \n    account value becomes insufficient to cover charges.\n\n5.4 The Money Market sub-account has a guaranteed minimum rate of \n    1.5% but other sub-accounts have no guaranteed minimum return.\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  SECTION 6: LOANS AND WITHDRAWALS                                 │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n6.1 POLICY LOANS:\n    • Maximum: 90% of surrender value\n    • Interest Rate: 5.5% per annum (fixed)\n    • Loan amounts are moved to the Money Market sub-account\n    • Reduces death benefit dollar-for-dollar\n\n6.2 PARTIAL WITHDRAWALS:\n    • Minimum: $1,000\n    • Maximum: Account value minus $5,000\n    • Processing fee: $50\n    • Surrender charges may apply (see Section 3.6)\n    • Reduces face amount proportionally\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  SECTION 7: POLICY LAPSE AND REINSTATEMENT                        │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n7.1 If account value is insufficient to cover monthly deductions","summary":"This document details critical aspects of a variable life insurance policy, including two death benefit choices—Level and Variable—with differing charge structures and growth potentials. Under the Variable option, benefits rise with account performance but carry non-guaranteed fluctuations due to market risk. Policy loans up to 90% of surrender value at a fixed 5.5% interest reduce the death benefit directly. Partial withdrawals require a $1,000 minimum and incur a $50 fee; they lower the face amount proportionally. Insufficient funds may trigger policy lapse unless reinstated with proof of insurability and additional payments.","topics":["Death Benefit Options","Investment Risk","Policy Loans","Withdrawal Rules"],"facts":[{"name":"Level Death Benefit","sentence":"Option I provides a level death benefit equal to the face amount.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Option I","Face Amount","Death Benefit"],"entities":[{"name":"Level Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Fixed payout option","relational_anchors":["Face Amount"]},{"name":"Variable Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Growth-linked payout option","relational_anchors":["Face Amount + Account Value","CURRENTLY SELECTED"]},{"name":"Proof of insurability","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Requirement for plan change","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Minimum face amount requirements","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Eligibility condition for switching","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$50 administrative fee","type":"FEE","role":"Cost for changing benefit option","relational_anchors":["50"]},{"name":"Investment risk","type":"RISK","role":"Borne solely by policy owner","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Account value fluctuations","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Non-guaranteed variable component","relational_anchors":["sub-account performance"]},{"name":"Policy lapse due to low account value","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Consequence of charge shortfall","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Money Market sub-account","type":"SUB_ACCOUNT","role":"Guaranteed-rate holding vehicle","relational_anchors":["guaranteed minimum rate of 1.5%","loan amounts are moved here"]},{"name":"5.5% per annum","type":"RATE","role":"Fixed interest rate on policy loans","relational_anchors":["Interest Rate: 5.5%"]},{"name":"Maximum: 90% of surrender value","type":"LIMIT","role":"Cap on allowable policy loan size","relational_anchors":["90%"]},{"name":"Reduces death benefit dollar-for-dollar","type":"DEDUCTION","role":"Impact of policy loan usage","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Partial Withdrawals","type":"WITHDRAWAL","role":"Reduced access to funds","relational_anchors":["Minimum: $1,000","Maximum: Account value minus $5,000","Processing fee: $50"]},{"name":"$50 processing fee","type":"FEE","role":"Charge for partial withdrawal","relational_anchors":["50"]},{"name":"Surrender charges","type":"CHARGE","role":"Potential cost during withdrawal","relational_anchors":["see Section 3.6"]},{"name":"Reduces face amount proportionally","type":"REDUCTION","role":"Effect of partial withdrawal","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Lower Charges: Option I","sentence":"Option I has lower charges compared to Option II.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Death Benefit Options","Charges Comparison","Policy Cost Structure"],"entities":[{"name":"Level Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Fixed payout option","relational_anchors":["Face Amount"]},{"name":"Variable Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Growth-linked payout option","relational_anchors":["Face Amount + Account Value","CURRENTLY SELECTED"]},{"name":"Proof of insurability","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Requirement for plan change","relational_anchors"