      <data key="d3">The initial face amount of $1 million serves as the foundational component of the death benefit under Option II, which adds the accumulated account value to it.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6f5fd4c3-4d4e-467b-8e2b-426f62766921" target="3aa92416-01dc-4fb4-901b-04bf91ba4c2b">
      <data key="d3">The initial face amount of $1 million establishes the sum payable at death, which directly applies to the primary beneficiary, Michael Thomas Foster, as specified in the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6f5fd4c3-4d4e-467b-8e2b-426f62766921" target="2a9798d0-4ad9-4bcf-9e30-219824f873d8">
      <data key="d3">The initial death benefit of $1 million is significant because it determines the payout amount if Dr. Amanda Katherine Foster passes away, and since her spouse Michael Thomas Foster is named as the primary beneficiary, he would receive this sum.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
