      <data key="d3">Death Benefit Option II defines the payout terms associated with the policy identified by Policy Number PIL-VUL-2024-5521.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="2f04250e-4053-4425-950f-f3efb61e460a">
      <data key="d3">Death Benefit Option II defines the terms of the payout at death, which became active as of the Policy Date—April 5, 2024—marking the beginning of its enforceability.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="673f04b9-0b00-413b-9fe0-acc4d73bc0db">
      <data key="d3">Option II, the chosen death benefit provision, applies exclusively to the insured party, Dr. Amanda Katherine Foster, defining the payout terms specific to her policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">associated with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="6f5fd4c3-4d4e-467b-8e2b-426f62766921">
      <data key="d3">Option II defines the method by which the death benefit is paid, including the base face amount; therefore, its applicability relies on the presence of a defined initial face amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="ebbf5cd2-4a0e-4c96-a21c-71b0ce22c1d2">
      <data key="d3">Choosing Death Benefit Option II influences the overall cost structure of the policy, including the expected payment of $12,000 annually, ensuring sufficient funding for the specified payout mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">The statement identifies Option II as the chosen death benefit provision, while the second sentence clarifies its definition by specifying how the payout is calculated as the sum of the face amount and accumulated account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="3aa92416-01dc-4fb4-901b-04bf91ba4c2b">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Death Benefit Option II defines the terms under which the primary beneficiary, Michael Thomas Foster, would receive the policy’s payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="ee48c30b-3bf6-4f6b-acb3-b55f04f44cd8">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Death Benefit Option II establishes the payout terms upon death, which complements the designation of a secondary beneficiary. This ensures that beneficiaries receive the specified benefit according to the plan’s structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433">
      <data key="d3">Option II determines how the death benefit is paid out, incorporating accumulated account value; Accumulation Units represent the underlying investment units contributing to this growth before distribution.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="de306b66-0150-43cd-a96c-13419925c4f3">
      <data key="d3">Option II determines how the death benefit is paid out, including the accumulation of account value over time. Unit value being recalculated daily reflects ongoing changes in investment performance that contribute to this accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7">
      <data key="d3">Option II's death benefit relies on the accumulated account value, which is determined by the performance and valuation of units within sub-accounts. Therefore, understanding unit value is essential to calculating the total payout under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad">
      <data key="d3">Option II determines the death benefit calculation based on the sum of the face amount and accumulated account value, while the daily M&amp;E charge reduces the growth potential of the account value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies Option II as the selected death benefit choice, and fact_sentence_2 verifies its ongoing selection, supporting consistency in policy configuration.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Option II’s death benefit depends on the accumulation of account value, which fluctuates according to investment performance within sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Option II's death benefit depends on investment gains within sub-accounts, meaning its final payout can increase or decrease based on financial market outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that Option II applies to this policy, and fact_sentence_2 explains that Option II delivers a variable death benefit based on face amount and account value, reinforcing the operational meaning of Option II within the policy framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II implies a non-guaranteed account value, meaning the accumulation depends on market performance rather than being assured by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that Option II is chosen, and fact_sentence_2 specifies that its death benefit grows with the account value, confirming the dynamic nature of the payout under this option.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies Option II as the selected death benefit choice, and fact_sentence_2 explains that this option does not guarantee the death benefit due to market-linked performance. Together, they clarify that the benefit depends on account value changes rather than being fixed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">Option II provides a death benefit equal to the face amount plus account value, but policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, thereby diminishing the final payout available to beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Death Benefit Option II influences how partial withdrawals affect the policy's financial structure by reducing the face amount proportionally when funds are withdrawn.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
