    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="3aa92416-01dc-4fb4-901b-04bf91ba4c2b">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit formula under Option II determines the total payout available at death. This payout is directed to the designated primary beneficiary, Michael Thomas Foster.</data>
      <data key="d4">entitled to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="85d2239e-5427-43be-b9c3-62f248d4781e">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II is determined by adding the face amount and accumulated account value. This total benefit is fully allocated to the primary beneficiary, who holds 100% ownership interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="de306b66-0150-43cd-a96c-13419925c4f3">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II is defined by adding the face amount and account value; however, this total relies on accurate valuations that depend on daily updates from fund performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II depends on the total account value, which is derived from the accumulation of units across sub-accounts, each having its own unit value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit formula under Option II determines what beneficiaries receive upon the insured's passing. This outcome depends on the total account value, which accumulates from premium allocations made over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II depends on the sum of the face amount and the account value, which is reduced by the ongoing Mortality and Expense Risk Charge of 0.90% annually.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The active selection of Option II ensures that the death benefit will be calculated as the sum of the face amount and the account value, aligning the policy’s payout rule with its current configuration.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that Option II's death benefit combines face amount and account value, while fact_sentence_2 explains how it increases over time as the account value rises, reinforcing the dynamic nature of the benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II relies on the account value, which is subject to market-driven changes and thus not guaranteed, making the final payout uncertain despite a clear calculation method.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The first statement defines how the death benefit is calculated under Option II, while the second explains that this calculated benefit is subject to market risks and thus not guaranteed, emphasizing the conditional nature of the payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that Option II’s death benefit combines the face amount and account value, which aligns exactly with fact_sentence_2's assertion that the benefit is the sum of these elements, reinforcing the same definition.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
