      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II relies on the account value, which changes based on sub-account performance, meaning its ultimate size is contingent on investment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Option II's death benefit, defined as face amount plus account value, increases when sub-account investments perform well, making its final payout dependent on market-driven gains.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
