    <edge source="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">The concept of unit value influences the growth of the account balance used in determining the death benefit under Option II, making it relevant to the option’s payout mechanics.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">The unit value determines the worth of investments in sub-accounts, contributing directly to the overall account value that increases the death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7" target="f655db57-9079-41c0-80b8-f555479b92bd">
      <data key="d3">The Unit Value represents the market-driven worth of each share in a Sub-Account, reflecting how much one unit of the allocated mutual fund is valued at any given time.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7" target="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433">
      <data key="d3">Unit Value defines the price per unit in a sub-account, which directly affects how much each Accumulation Unit is worth. Without knowing the unit value, the actual value of accumulation units cannot be determined.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7" target="de306b66-0150-43cd-a96c-13419925c4f3">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Unit Value, defined as the worth of one unit in a sub-account, relies on daily recalculations driven by underlying fund performance to reflect current market conditions accurately.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">Unit Value represents the price per share of investments within sub-accounts; it is reduced annually due to the 0.90% Mortality and Expense Risk Charge applied to the account's value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7" target="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df">
      <data key="d3">The value of one unit in a sub-account determines how effectively premium payments translate into actual investments once loaded fees are deducted. Without knowing the unit value, it would not be possible to calculate how many units are acquired from incoming premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
