    <edge source="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433" target="ebbf5cd2-4a0e-4c96-a21c-71b0ce22c1d2">
      <data key="d3">Accumulation Units are created when premiums are allocated to sub-accounts, so they depend on the payment of the planned annual premium to exist.</data>
      <data key="d4">depended on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Accumulation Units explains how funds grow within sub-accounts, forming part of the account value used in calculating the death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433" target="f655db57-9079-41c0-80b8-f555479b92bd">
      <data key="d3">Accumulation Units are units held inside Sub-Accounts, which are defined as segregated accounts investing in specific mutual funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">contains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433" target="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7">
      <data key="d3">Accumulation Units are measured by their quantity multiplied by the Unit Value, meaning they rely entirely on unit value for valuation. Therefore, unit value provides the foundational metric used to assess accumulation units.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in valuation of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433" target="de306b66-0150-43cd-a96c-13419925c4f3">
      <data key="d3">Accumulation Units exist in sub-accounts and derive their value from daily Unit Value adjustments based on fund performance. Their existence relies on ongoing valuation mechanisms defined by unit value computation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">Accumulation Units represent investment holdings in sub-accounts before payouts occur, while the M&amp;E charge of 0.90% applies to these accounts annually as a cost of insurance coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433" target="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df">
      <data key="d3">Premiums paid are first reduced by the loading fee, then assigned to sub-accounts, forming Accumulation Units. These units represent the invested portion of premiums before any payouts or withdrawals occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
