    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="ebbf5cd2-4a0e-4c96-a21c-71b0ce22c1d2">
      <data key="d3">Daily deduction of the M&amp;E charge influences how effectively the annual premium contributes to growth, though the premium itself remains unchanged regardless of fee frequency.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">The daily charging of the M&amp;E risk fee impacts the account’s growth rate, thereby affecting the total accumulated value used in calculating the death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="de306b66-0150-43cd-a96c-13419925c4f3">
      <data key="d3">The daily deduction of the Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reduces the account value, thereby impacting the underlying assets used to calculate the unit value each day.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">The daily application of the Mortality and Expense Risk Charge aligns with the stated annual rate of 0.90%, ensuring the cumulative impact matches the yearly figure through regular compounding.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="15773119-4ea5-47b0-8cfd-6116e4cb5765">
      <data key="d3">The daily application of the M&amp;E charge ensures that insurance risks and administrative costs are consistently covered over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The daily application of the Mortality and Expense Risk Charge requires the activation of Option II, making the charge contingent on this choice.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The daily application of the Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reduces the account value over time, thereby affecting the variable death benefit outlined in Option II, which depends on the combined face amount and account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">The daily application of the Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reflects the operational cost associated with maintaining a non-guaranteed account value under Option II, ensuring the insurer can manage risk despite volatile investment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The daily application of the Mortality and Expense Risk Charge sustains the financial framework underlying Option II, which inherently lacks a guaranteed death benefit due to its exposure to market-driven account value changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">The daily application of the Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reduces the account value, thereby influencing the magnitude of the variable death benefit under Option II, which depends on sub-account performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">The daily Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reduces the account value, which limits the rate at which the death benefit under Option II can increase. Without these deductions, the death benefit would grow more rapidly.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The daily M&amp;E charge reduces the account value over time, counteracting potential growth driven by favorable sub-account performance described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">The daily M&amp;E charge erodes the policy’s account value, reducing potential growth available to offset reductions from loans. As loans decrease the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, the compounding effect of fees like M&amp;E can accelerate the erosion of coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">compounds with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The daily charging of the Mortality and Expense Risk Fee gradually erodes the policy’s account value, thereby increasing the relative impact of any partial withdrawal on the remaining face amount. As such, frequent or large withdrawals compound the financial pressure caused by these recurring charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
