      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual Mortality and Expense Risk Charge applies to the policy owned by Dr. Amanda Katherine Foster.</data>
      <data key="d4">associated with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reduces the growth of the account value, thereby affecting the final amount added to the face amount in determining the total death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% Annual M&amp;E Charge systematically lowers the account’s value, thereby affecting the Unit Value of each sub-account over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433">
      <data key="d3">The annual M&amp;E risk charge of 0.90% affects the performance of sub-account investments where Accumulation Units are held, reducing overall account value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad">
      <data key="d3">The annual rate of 0.90% reflects the total cost imposed on the policyholder, which is realized through daily charges distributed across each day of the year.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="15773119-4ea5-47b0-8cfd-6116e4cb5765">
      <data key="d3">The annual M&amp;E charge of 0.90% serves to cover underlying insurance risks and administrative expenses associated with the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual M&amp;E risk charge reduces the net premium available for investment, affecting how much of the paid premium gets allocated to sub-accounts after loading fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the 0.90% M&amp;E charge, which is applicable only when Option II is selected, confirming its operational status based on fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% M&amp;E charge reduces the account value annually, and since the account value fluctuates with sub-account performance, the real-world financial effect of this charge varies accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reduces the account’s growth potential, thereby influencing how quickly the death benefit under Option II can increase alongside the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% Mortality and Expense Risk Charge reduces the account value over time, thereby affecting the variable portion of the death benefit defined by Option II. This charge is integral to calculating the net accumulation supporting the total payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% mortality and expense charge applies to the account value, which under Option II is not guaranteed and can vary due to market conditions. Thus, the cost burden is realized within an unstable asset base.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% M&amp;E charge applies uniformly to the policy’s account value, which directly influences the fluctuating death benefit under Option II by reducing available funds over time despite market gains.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% Mortality and Expense Risk Charge erodes the account value over time, reducing the potential growth of the death benefit under Option II, which is already non-guaranteed. This financial drag increases the likelihood that the final payout could fall short of expectations.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% Mortality and Expense Risk Charge impacts the account value used to determine the proportional reduction in face amount when partial withdrawals occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% mortality and expense risk charge influences the growth of the policy's cash value over time, which determines the surrender value used to calculate the maximum allowable loan. As loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, the impact of the M&amp;E charge on account value ultimately constrains the total borrowable amount and therefore shapes how much the death benefit can be diminished through borrowing.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
