    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="2caeaed3-b5b6-41bc-8789-ddf838e37589">
      <data key="d3">The method of allocating premium payments to sub-accounts after the premium load depends on the specific policy instance identified by the policy number, ensuring accurate tracking and administration.</data>
      <data key="d4">references</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="2f04250e-4053-4425-950f-f3efb61e460a">
      <data key="d3">Allocation of premiums to sub-accounts happens only after the policy has been formally established; therefore, the policy date precedes any such fund distribution.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="673f04b9-0b00-413b-9fe0-acc4d73bc0db">
      <data key="d3">Premiums being allocated to sub-accounts after applying a premium load relies on the policyholder’s identity—Dr. Amanda Katherine Foster—as the individual whose contributions fund those investments.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="06a215da-3e37-426f-927c-aa13bfca7a81">
      <data key="d3">Premiums are first reduced by a load based on the insured’s class; since the insured is classified as "Preferred Plus," this affects the portion that gets allocated to sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">modified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="6f5fd4c3-4d4e-467b-8e2b-426f62766921">
      <data key="d3">Premiums paid by the insured are used to fund the policy’s growth via sub-account investments, which contribute to building cash value supporting the eventual payout equal to the face amount at death.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="ebbf5cd2-4a0e-4c96-a21c-71b0ce22c1d2">
      <data key="d3">After being applied to the policy, the premium payments are directed into sub-accounts, meaning the allocation process depends on the existence of scheduled premium contributions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">Premiums paid are first subject to loads before being assigned to investment sub-accounts. These investments contribute to the growing account value that ultimately increases the death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="f655db57-9079-41c0-80b8-f555479b92bd">
      <data key="d3">Premium payments are first reduced by a loading fee before being assigned to sub-accounts, which are specifically designed to hold investments in mutual funds as outlined in the policy’s structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="fcdeb251-2bd8-4d1c-99e4-7dccc6341fb7">
      <data key="d3">Premium allocations to sub-accounts depend on the unit value; higher or lower unit prices affect the number of units received per dollar paid after loading charges, making unit value essential for determining investment impact.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="de306b66-0150-43cd-a96c-13419925c4f3">
      <data key="d3">Premiums are first reduced by a load before being assigned to sub-accounts, whose valuations depend on daily unit value updates driven by fund performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="d75d6f5b-d1c8-41ad-b706-f720effdd433">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premium payments to sub-accounts results in the creation of Accumulation Units, which serve as the foundational unit of measurement for investment growth within those accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="15773119-4ea5-47b0-8cfd-6116e4cb5765">
      <data key="d3">Premiums are reduced by the M&amp;E charge before being allocated to sub-accounts, meaning the charge determines how much capital enters the investment component.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">Allocating premium payments to sub-accounts occurs only after deducting charges like the M&amp;E fee; thus, the timing and magnitude of allocations depend on the presence of such ongoing expenses.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The current selection of Option II ensures that premium payments are directed into sub-accounts post-load deduction, enabling investment-linked growth potential consistent with the policy’s variable benefit structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to sub-accounts after applying the premium load contributes to building the account value, which directly increases the variable death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Premiums are directed to sub-accounts post-load deduction, enabling the account value under Option II to grow or decline based on those investments' performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Premium allocations to sub-accounts after loading enable investment growth, which directly contributes to the increasing death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to volatile sub-accounts under Option II leads to non-guaranteed account values, meaning the funded amounts can fluctuate based on market conditions rather than being secured.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to sub-accounts after loading contributes to the variable performance of the death benefit under Option II, explaining why it is not guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Premiums paid after loading are invested in sub-accounts, whose performance determines the fluctuating death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">Premiums increase the account value by funding sub-accounts, which indirectly supports the base for proportional reductions when partial withdrawals occur.</data>
