    </edge>
    <edge source="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead" target="f87f876d-e28c-4a7b-87ed-5807405fbff7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">percentage range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead" target="d636dd34-6b7b-47a4-af86-f861e5275aa8">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">charge schedule</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead" target="81e49cb2-9973-4f29-93f9-b747d6bd02ec">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a 5.0% premium load directly explains why premiums are reduced before allocation—the load acts as an upfront deduction from each payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead" target="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef">
      <data key="d3">The 5% premium load is applied before any allocation takes place; once this deduction is made, the residual funds become available for distribution among investment sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead" target="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5">
      <data key="d3">The 5% premium load reduces the net amount available for investment, shaping the pool from which allocations to sub-accounts are made. This loaded amount determines the scale of investments guided by investor directives.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.875</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead" target="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281">
      <data key="d3">The 5% premium load ensures initial capital is directed into available sub-accounts like the Equity Growth Fund, enabling investors to begin allocating funds under specified guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead" target="c6b46ac7-78f4-449c-8b45-6fd65adfbba6">
      <data key="d3">The 5% premium load impacts how much capital enters the account, influencing overall asset allocation capacity. This foundational step enables investors to direct funds into available sub-accounts, such as the Balanced Allocation Fund, which is explicitly listed among the investment choices.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="dc984f1a-e6b6-45e4-8e32-568453780178" target="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to premium load</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="38b9d13e-6477-4e71-b12f-f1ef25322704" target="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to premium load</data>
    </edge>
