    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="81e49cb2-9973-4f29-93f9-b747d6bd02ec">
      <data key="d3">Allocations to sub-accounts depend on the portion of the premium left after the loading has been deducted; thus, the allocation cannot occur until the load is applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="49459120-af42-471a-a0d9-d0ea5424bead">
      <data key="d3">Allocation of premium payments to sub-accounts follows directly from the deduction of the 5% loading, making the initial loading a prerequisite step.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-load premiums enables investment in designated sub-accounts like the Equity Growth Fund, which is explicitly listed among the options.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5">
      <data key="d3">After accounting for the 5% loading, premiums are distributed among sub-accounts; this distribution is governed by the investor’s specified investment preferences.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="c6b46ac7-78f4-449c-8b45-6fd65adfbba6">
      <data key="d3">The allocation process described in sentence 1 enables investment in various sub-accounts, including the Balanced Allocation Fund mentioned in sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="0ec4db95-1572-487f-90d2-c5a822614352">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loading premiums occurs across multiple sub-accounts, including the Government Bond Fund, which is explicitly listed among the investment choices.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="452470ff-1e32-43f1-8de7-0e950227006a">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-load premiums to sub-accounts includes various investment options, among them the International Equity Fund, which serves as a concrete instance of how capital may be distributed.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="a6548f00-c863-44e8-a21a-b412497ba0bc">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-load premiums occurs across multiple sub-accounts, including the Money Market Fund, which is explicitly listed among the options.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="5471d238-37e9-4478-8504-a41c8fe37a7b">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loading premiums to sub-accounts enables the distribution reflected in current investment splits, such as the 40% assigned to the Equity Growth Fund.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="711e0816-e0bc-445f-966b-4be7ac86e87f">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loading premiums to sub-accounts includes assigning 10% to the Money Market Fund, reflecting one component of the overall distribution strategy outlined in the initial statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="c2037215-53c9-4630-94af-e8bb4930956c">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loaded premiums to sub-accounts enables investors to direct funds into various investment vehicles, including specialized ones like the Real Estate Securities Fund.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="3014df8f-db7d-4af8-9b3e-fa9f179736e5">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loading premiums to sub-accounts enables investors to distribute funds into designated categories like the Balanced Allocation Fund, which currently holds 30% of assets.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="3e851cbd-ccf3-4477-9f3d-4f20316c7521">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of funds into sub-accounts follows premium loading, enabling investment direction per investor choice. This setup supports the ability to alter investments dynamically.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="09cdc94b-7cd3-44a1-8084-8305f1696fe3">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how post-loading premiums are distributed among sub-accounts. The second sentence specifies the current proportion assigned to the Government Bond Fund, which is part of the overall allocation strategy but not directly derived from the allocation mechanism described earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="3bfbc615-fc3f-4d02-a8b2-3b08079b9159">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of funds occurs after applying the premium load, and any modifications to these allocations may be initiated using the online portal.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="e9a445fa-2366-4834-8a4b-4421c9a31eb0">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loaded premiums to sub-accounts sets the stage for any future modifications. Changes to these allocations may be initiated through formal requests, allowing investors to adjust previously assigned amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="67c7a149-4651-4b13-989b-a037490c835d">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loading premiums into sub-accounts enables investors to manage their portfolio, supporting the freedom to adjust investments up to 12 times annually without fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="7d291689-a55d-42fe-bd85-5cc34da20262">
      <data key="d3">The ability to allocate post-load premiums into sub-accounts allows investors to adjust investments, enabling the imposition of a $25 fee when changes exceed 12 annually.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loaded premiums to sub-accounts sets the foundation for account value accumulation, which directly influences the calculation basis for the 0.90% annual mortality and expense risk charge.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="89409c54-bed8-4ec7-9f17-d30aaecf68d3">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loaded premiums to sub-accounts sets the context for understanding investment costs; detailed expense ratios for these sub-accounts are documented separately in the prospectus.</data>
      <data key="d4">supplements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">After applying the 5% loading, premiums are directed into specific sub-accounts, which incur varying annual expense ratios ranging from 0.45% to 1.25%.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">After applying the 5% loading, premium amounts are assigned to various sub-accounts per investor instructions. Each such sub-account carries an independent annual expense ratio, contributing to overall investment costs.</data>
      <data key="d4">allocated to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premium payments to sub-accounts determines the account value, which directly influences the variable death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Allocating premiums to sub-accounts enables investment growth, which directly contributes to the rising account value that fuels the increasing death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Remaining premium payments directed into sub-accounts influence the performance of those accounts, which directly impacts the fluctuating death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Remaining premiums are directed into sub-accounts per investor instructions, and since these sub-accounts' returns determine the account value under Option II, this allocation directly affects its fluctuation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to sub-accounts influences the pool from which partial withdrawals are drawn, meaning ongoing contributions impact the availability of funds subject to withdrawal limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of post-loading premiums to sub-accounts influences the underlying investments that determine the variable death benefit under Option II, linking payment strategy to potential payout variability.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to sub-accounts influences long-term investment outcomes, where underperformance risks causing the policy to lapse due to insufficient accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Allocating remaining premiums to sub-accounts impacts the account's ability to sustain monthly deductions, potentially leading to lapses if returns are inadequate.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">Remaining premium payments are directed into sub-accounts after initial loads, while partial withdrawals decrease the face amount proportionally, affecting long-term benefit levels and potentially altering future allocation capacity.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The rule governing premium allocation to sub-accounts influences long-term account value, which affects the basis for calculating surrender charges upon partial withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
