    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="5471d238-37e9-4478-8504-a41c8fe37a7b">
      <data key="d3">Investor directives determine how funds are distributed among sub-accounts; the 40% allocation to the Equity Growth Fund is one concrete result of those instructions.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="3014df8f-db7d-4af8-9b3e-fa9f179736e5">
      <data key="d3">The investor’s directive determines how funds are distributed among sub-accounts, and the 30% allocation to the Balanced Allocation Fund exemplifies this process in practice.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="e9a445fa-2366-4834-8a4b-4421c9a31eb0">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations depend on formal submission methods; changes require a written request to be processed.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="c2037215-53c9-4630-94af-e8bb4930956c">
      <data key="d3">The rule governing how funds are distributed among sub-accounts aligns with investor-directed choices, and one such option available under those directions is the Real Estate Securities Fund.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="09cdc94b-7cd3-44a1-8084-8305f1696fe3">
      <data key="d3">Investor directives govern how premiums are assigned among sub-accounts, and the 20% allocation to the Government Bond Fund reflects one such directive being implemented.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="711e0816-e0bc-445f-966b-4be7ac86e87f">
      <data key="d3">The allocation to sub-accounts is determined by investor directives, and the current 10% holding in the Money Market Fund illustrates one application of those instructions.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="3e851cbd-ccf3-4477-9f3d-4f20316c7521">
      <data key="d3">The rule that allocations follow investor instructions enables the flexibility described in the second sentence, allowing investors to adjust investments as desired.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="3bfbc615-fc3f-4d02-a8b2-3b08079b9159">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations require a method to submit changes, and the online portal provides that access point for modifying investments within the specified limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="67c7a149-4651-4b13-989b-a037490c835d">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocation rules enable flexible reallocation decisions, making it possible to implement frequent changes without financial penalties within the allowed limit.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="7d291689-a55d-42fe-bd85-5cc34da20262">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocation allows flexibility in choosing sub-accounts, but excessive modifications trigger additional fees due to administrative overhead.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations assign funds to specific sub-accounts, each of which independently applies its own annual expense ratio as part of operating costs.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations determine which sub-accounts receive funds, each carrying its own expense ratio ranging from 0.45% to 1.25%. This means the chosen distribution affects overall cost burden.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="89409c54-bed8-4ec7-9f17-d30aaecf68d3">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations to sub-accounts require knowledge of associated expenses; thus, access to detailed expense ratios enhances informed decision-making regarding asset distribution.</data>
      <data key="d4">supplements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations to sub-accounts determine the account value growth, which directly impacts the increasing death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums into sub-accounts, as directed by the investor, determines the account value that contributes to the variable death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations to sub-accounts determine the performance basis for the variable death benefit under Option II, making the distribution method essential to its fluctuation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations into sub-accounts determine how the account value under Option II responds to market movements, making the distribution method foundational to its performance-based valuation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations into volatile sub-accounts influence the variable death benefit under Option II, making the outcome dependent on investment performance rather than being fixed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The rule that investments follow investor instructions enables personalized portfolio construction, which supports the ability to make meaningful partial withdrawals by maintaining sufficient accumulated value across sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The allocation rules govern how premiums are invested, which affects the available cash value used when calculating reductions from partial withdrawals. Thus, proper allocation impacts the basis upon which face amounts are reduced during withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Proper allocation of premiums into higher-performing sub-accounts helps maintain sufficient account value, reducing the likelihood of the policy lapsing due to inadequate funding.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocations to sub-accounts may be affected by surrender charges when partial withdrawals occur, linking investment control to potential penalties upon exiting portions of those investments.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">Investor-directed allocation into sub-accounts determines the policy’s investment performance; weak returns from these investments can deplete reserves and increase the risk of policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="473ed7df-33ad-457f-ab28-2fbf5ec83cdf" target="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
