      <data key="d3">The presence of the Equity Growth Fund as a sub-account provides one of the possible choices for reallocation. This option becomes actionable when investors use the online portal to adjust their portfolio assignments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281" target="7d291689-a55d-42fe-bd85-5cc34da20262">
      <data key="d3">The existence of the Equity Growth Fund enables investors to allocate funds into it; however, making more than 12 such adjustments annually incurs a $25 fee per additional change.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">The availability of the Equity Growth Fund as a sub-account supports the assertion that each sub-account carries its own distinct annual expense ratio, reinforcing the idea of differentiated cost structures within the investment options.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
