    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality and expense risk charge depends on the account value derived from prior premium allocations to sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">drives</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="f32fd9d4-462b-417e-9c50-f00a3ce78b9b">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual Mortality &amp; Expense Risk Charge is applied by deducting a portion of the account value each day, ensuring consistent accrual throughout the year.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">The mortality risk charge is a uniform percentage-based fee applied annually to the entire account value regardless of sub-account allocation. In contrast, individual sub-accounts incur additional expenses through varying internal expense ratios specific to each fund’s management.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">The mortality and expense risk charge is a flat 0.90% annual fee applied to the account value, independent of individual sub-account performance. This contrasts with sub-account expense ratios, which vary by fund and range from 0.45% to 1.25%.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality and expense charge reduces the account value incrementally, increasing the risk that the balance may not sustain required monthly deductions over extended periods, potentially leading to policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality charge reduces the account value over time, thereby affecting the variable portion of the death benefit under Option II, which is calculated as the sum of the face amount and account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality charge reduces the account value, thereby potentially limiting the growth of the death benefit under Option II, which rises with account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality risk charge reduces the account value available for investment in sub-accounts, indirectly affecting the growth potential underlying the fluctuating death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality risk charge scales with the account value, which itself fluctuates based on sub-account performance under Option II. Therefore, the charge's dollar impact varies alongside investment gains or losses.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality risk charge contributes to the total cost burden that could affect whether sufficient funds remain to support the non-guaranteed death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences cost</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality charge operates continuously regardless of transactions, whereas the $50 processing fee applies only during partial withdrawals. Both contribute to overall policy expenses but serve distinct purposes within the fee framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary fees</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality charge reduces the account value over time, potentially impacting the available balance for partial withdrawals that require a $1,000 minimum. Higher fees may limit liquidity by reducing accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality risk charge applies to the account value, which decreases when partial withdrawals occur, thereby reducing the basis for future charges. This creates a feedback loop where withdrawal activity influences ongoing cost exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality charge erodes the account value over time, increasing the likelihood that the balance will become insufficient to meet monthly deductions, potentially causing policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to lapse</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The 0.90% annual mortality charge reduces the account value over time, compounding pressure on policyholders during periods of weak investment returns, which increases the risk of policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">exacerbates risk</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="35e2c60a-0431-4fab-8353-d5e2aaa5ea51" target="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to mortality expense charge</data>
    </edge>
