    <edge source="f32fd9d4-462b-417e-9c50-f00a3ce78b9b" target="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33">
      <data key="d3">Daily deductions ensure that the total annual Mortality &amp; Expense Risk Charge accumulates precisely to 0.90% of the account value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f32fd9d4-462b-417e-9c50-f00a3ce78b9b" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d3">The Mortality &amp; Expense Risk Charge is deducted daily from the account balance, reflecting ongoing insurance costs that include the Cost of Insurance. This periodic deduction supports the implementation of the COI calculation derived from the face amount at risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f32fd9d4-462b-417e-9c50-f00a3ce78b9b" target="522644d7-e290-4908-b13c-663896d15b1c">
      <data key="d3">The Mortality &amp; Expense Risk Charge is calculated based on the Face Amount at Risk, which represents the difference between the death benefit and account value. This ensures that the charge reflects the insurer's exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f32fd9d4-462b-417e-9c50-f00a3ce78b9b" target="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2">
      <data key="d3">The daily deduction of the Mortality &amp; Expense Risk Charge reduces the account value incrementally, increasing the risk that the account may become insufficient to cover deductions for 61 consecutive days, potentially leading to policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="54c56e4d-4a22-4923-abb9-d1b47804cf91" target="f32fd9d4-462b-417e-9c50-f00a3ce78b9b">
