    </edge>
    <edge source="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf" target="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2">
      <data key="d3">The $15 monthly administrative charge reduces the account value, increasing the risk that the account may not sustain sufficient funds to meet ongoing deductions for 61 consecutive days, potentially triggering policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The $15 monthly administrative charge affects total policy expenses, indirectly influencing the account value used in calculating the variable death benefit under Option II by reducing net returns over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">The $15 monthly administrative charge reduces the account value over time, thereby slightly diminishing the pool available for growth that drives the increasing death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">The $15 monthly administrative charge sustains the infrastructure supporting the investment sub-accounts whose performance determines the fluctuating death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The $15 monthly administrative charge reduces the available account value, indirectly affecting the growth potential described in Option II’s variable benefit structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The $15 monthly administrative charge reduces the account value over time, increasing the risk that the balance will become too low to cover future deductions, potentially causing the policy to lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to lapse</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">A persistent $15 monthly administrative charge erodes policy value over time, compounding the impact of poor investment returns and raising the risk of insufficient funds leading to lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">exacerbates risk</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86a5ff07-8719-474b-8f8a-0145c8d177b6" target="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
    </edge>
