    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="f32fd9d4-462b-417e-9c50-f00a3ce78b9b">
      <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance is computed based on the face amount at risk and a monthly rate, forming part of the broader Mortality &amp; Expense Risk Charge, which is subsequently deducted daily from the policyholder’s account.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="522644d7-e290-4908-b13c-663896d15b1c">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of the Cost of Insurance depends directly on Face Amount at Risk, which itself is determined by subtracting the Account Value from the Death Benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of the Cost of Insurance depends on the face amount at risk, which fluctuates under Option II as the death benefit varies with account value, linking pricing mechanics to benefit design.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of the Cost of Insurance depends on the face amount at risk, which can fluctuate alongside the growing account value under Option II, thereby affecting periodic premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of the Cost of Insurance depends on the face amount at risk, which can increase alongside sub-account gains under Option II, leading to higher premiums when the death benefit rises due to strong investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">A reduction in the face amount due to partial withdrawals decreases the 'face amount at risk,' thereby lowering the cost of insurance as per the given formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of the Cost of Insurance relies on the face amount at risk, which is influenced by the account value that fluctuates with sub-account performance described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of the Cost of Insurance depends on the face amount at risk, which fluctuates under Option II where the death benefit is not guaranteed, making COI subject to market-related variations.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance increases when the face amount at risk rises, and partial withdrawals reduce that amount, thereby potentially lowering future COI expenses. The $50 processing fee adds an administrative burden linked to such reductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The cost of insurance depends on the face amount at risk, which decreases when partial withdrawals occur. Since partial withdrawals require a $1,000 minimum and reduce the face amount, they directly impact the basis used in calculating the COI.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The method for calculating the monthly Cost of Insurance (COI) affects the total deductions from the policy's account value, influencing whether it remains sufficient to avoid lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The calculation of the Cost of Insurance (COI) affects the depletion of the policy’s cash value; sustained low returns mean less growth to offset these recurring fees, raising the risk of policy lapse due to inadequate funding.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9ae3bbd-4829-49f2-b213-3a6544bb3038" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">defines</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bd4197ed-6469-4809-bfee-d8a22691d123" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">provides annual coi rate range</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8bb95592-f271-4a81-bbed-78fb66246d5f" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">defines tiered monthly coi rates by policy year</data>
    </edge>
