    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="3e851cbd-ccf3-4477-9f3d-4f20316c7521">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges create a constraint on free allocation changes by imposing penalties based on timing, thus limiting the practical freedom described in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2">
      <data key="d3">The general rule that surrender charges depend on a scheduled timeline is illustrated by the specific case where charges are set at 7% for premiums paid in the first two years.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a surrender charge schedule implies varying rates depending on policy duration; specifically, for premiums paid in Year 3–4, the applicable charge is set at 5%, illustrating one entry within the broader schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a surrender charge schedule implies varying rates depending on policy duration; specifically, for premiums paid in Year 5–6, the charge is set at 3%, illustrating an instance of the broader scheduling principle.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c">
      <data key="d3">The surrender charge schedule outlined in fact_sentence_1 includes exceptions, such as when premiums are paid in Year 7 or later, resulting in no surrender charge being applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional exception</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges may become significant if a policyholder considers withdrawing funds shortly after purchase, potentially exacerbating financial strain that could lead to failure in covering monthly deductions—thus increasing the risk of lapse under prolonged shortfalls.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional relationship</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges affect when investors might exit the policy, influencing whether the account value grows enough to maximize the variable death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Lower surrender charges over time encourage policyholders to retain coverage longer, allowing the account value—and thus the death benefit under Option II—to grow more fully through compounding returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges diminish over time, affecting exit timing, while the variable death benefit rises or falls with sub-account returns, meaning long-term holding could increase payout potential despite decreasing fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges depend on how long the policy has been held, and since the account value under Option II changes with sub-account returns, these fluctuations affect the surrender value and thus determine when and how much the surrender charge applies.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges affect early termination costs, while the lack of guarantee in Option II’s death benefit reflects market-driven variability in payouts. Both highlight non-fixed elements tied to policy duration and investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual relation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges affect the cost of exiting the policy early, while partial withdrawals have a minimum threshold and fee; together, these features govern liquidity and exit strategy within the policy framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact liquidity and withdrawal timing, potentially exacerbating financial strain from poor investment returns, which could increase the risk of policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a surrender charge schedule implies that early withdrawals—including partial ones—are subject to financial penalties, supporting the application of such charges during partial withdrawals as noted in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges relate to terminating the policy early, while the $50 processing fee applies only to partial withdrawals. Though both affect cash flow upon accessing policy value, they operate independently within different transaction types.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges influence when an investor might withdraw funds, potentially leading to reduced account value. If withdrawals occur frequently or excessively under these charges, it increases the risk of the account balance falling below required levels, triggering a potential policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply when withdrawing funds early, and since partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally, these actions may increase effective surrender fees relative to remaining value. This interaction highlights trade-offs between access to cash and sustained policy integrity.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4746af17-fbd8-4395-84b8-9f04c66aae0d" target="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to surrender charge schedule</data>
    </edge>
