    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="3e851cbd-ccf3-4477-9f3d-4f20316c7521">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply when investors alter their allocations early, limiting unrestricted access despite having the right to do so frequently.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="e9a445fa-2366-4834-8a4b-4421c9a31eb0">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges of 7% in Years 1–2 apply when reallocating funds, requiring formal submission through a written request process.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce">
      <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge applicable in Years 1–2 serves as an example of how the broader surrender charge schedule is implemented under the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that surrender charges are higher (7%) during the first two years, while fact sentence 2 indicates they drop to 5% in Years 3–4, showing a progressive reduction over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges decrease from 7% in Years 1–2 to 3% in Years 5–6, illustrating a gradual reduction over time as part of the policy’s declining surrender charge schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">declines over time</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges start high at 7% for early policy years but decrease over time, reaching zero from Year 7 onward due to scheduled reductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">High surrender charges in early years may discourage policyholders from keeping the policy long enough to fully benefit from the growing variable death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges in early years impact when investors exit the policy, potentially affecting long-term exposure to sub-account performance that determines the variable death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge applies when withdrawing early, particularly affecting accounts whose value fluctuates with sub-account performance, such as those under Option II described here.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge in early years discourages premature withdrawals, helping preserve account value needed to meet recurring deductions and prevent policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge applies when policies are terminated early, potentially discouraging actions like partial withdrawals that also impact the policy's value and face amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge in Years 1–2 applies if a policyholder terminates coverage early, whereas partial withdrawals above $1,000 allow continued access to funds without full cancellation. The two provisions together define financial consequences tied to different types of cash-out actions.</data>
      <data key="d4">complies with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">High surrender charges in early years discourage policyholders from accessing funds, increasing reliance on consistent investment performance. If investments perform poorly, lack of liquidity due to surrender fees raises the likelihood of policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">exacerbates risk</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge for premium payments in Years 1–2 applies specifically to early withdrawals, including partial ones, consistent with the rule stated in fact_sentence_2 regarding applicable penalties.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge in Years 1–2 applies to full surrenders or significant withdrawals that terminate coverage, while the $50 processing fee is charged per partial withdrawal regardless of timing. These represent distinct types of withdrawal fees operating under different conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">compliments with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
