      <data key="d3">Surrender charges decrease from 5% in Years 3–4 to 3% in Years 5–6, reflecting a progressive reduction over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges decrease from 5% in Years 3–4 to 0% when premiums are paid in Year 7 or later, reflecting a time-based reduction schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges in later years affect whether investors retain ownership long enough to benefit from a growing variable death benefit linked to account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">A 5% surrender charge in Years 3–4 affects the financial viability of exiting the policy, potentially influencing whether investors retain coverage long enough for the variable death benefit under Option II to grow meaningfully through sub-account gains.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The 5% surrender charge applies to early withdrawals from an account whose value fluctuates with sub-account performance, meaning the effective cost of exiting depends on how well investments have performed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The 5% surrender charge for premiums paid in Years 3–4 applies when early withdrawals occur, consistent with the general rule that partial withdrawals incur surrender charges per Section 3.6.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The 5% surrender charge in Years 3–4 affects overall policy flexibility, potentially influencing decisions about making partial withdrawals, especially when considering associated fees like the $50 charge mentioned in Chunk Summary 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The 5% surrender charge in Years 3–4 reflects a penalty for terminating the policy early, while the $50 fee for partial withdrawals applies when reducing the policy's cash value incrementally. Both represent financial disincentives tied to access to accumulated value, though under different circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The 5% surrender charge in Years 3–4 may discourage premature withdrawals, helping maintain sufficient account value to avoid lapses from unpaid fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">A 5% surrender charge in Years 3–4 discourages early exits, potentially forcing investors to endure poor performance rather than withdraw, increasing the likelihood of policy lapse if investments fail.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
