      <data key="d3">A 3% surrender charge in Years 5–6 impacts investors who exit before maturity, potentially affecting long-term exposure to sub-accounts whose performance drives the variable death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The 3% surrender charge in Years 5–6 applies to withdrawals from an account whose value fluctuates with sub-account performance, meaning the actual loss incurred depends on both market outcomes and contract terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The 3% surrender charge applies when terminating the policy early, while partial withdrawals above $1,000 allow limited access to funds without full surrender. These provisions together shape how policyholders manage liquidity before maturity.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The 3% surrender charge applicable to premiums paid in Years 5–6 supports the broader rule that surrender charges apply to certain transactions like partial withdrawals, suggesting consistency in penalty application across transaction types.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The 3% surrender charge in Years 5–6 discourages premature withdrawals, helping preserve account value needed to meet monthly deduction requirements and reducing the risk of policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The 3% surrender charge in Years 5–6 reflects a penalty for terminating coverage early, while the $50 fee for partial withdrawals represents a separate cost associated with reducing policy value incrementally. Both relate to financial consequences when accessing accumulated cash value before maturity.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">A 3% surrender charge in Years 5–6 may discourage early withdrawals despite poor investment performance, potentially contributing to policy lapse if insufficient funds remain.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
