    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="3e851cbd-ccf3-4477-9f3d-4f20316c7521">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges being zero for premiums paid in Year 7 or later enable investors to alter their investment allocations freely, enhancing the practicality of the stated policy allowing unlimited modifications.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce">
      <data key="d3">When premiums are paid in Year 7 or later, they fall under the exemption clause of the surrender charge schedule described in fact_sentence_1, rendering the charge null.</data>
      <data key="d4">exempt from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2">
      <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges from Year 7 onward implies they were previously applicable—such as the 7% rate in Years 1–2—as part of a phased reduction schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130">
      <data key="d3">The elimination of surrender charges after Year 7 implies they were previously active—such as the 5% rate applicable during Years 3–4—as part of a phased decline.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476">
      <data key="d3">The elimination of surrender charges after Year 6 follows logically from earlier years' higher charges, showing a progressive phase-out tied to policy duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges from Year 7 onward allows greater flexibility for investors to maintain or grow their account value, enhancing the potential upside of Option II’s variable death benefit, which depends on such growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Once surrender charges end in Year 7, policyholders can fully utilize account gains from investments, enabling greater growth in the death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances growth under</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Surrender charges being eliminated from Year 7 onward allow investors more flexibility to access funds without penalty, enabling them to potentially realize gains from sub-account performance reflected in the variable death benefit under Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The zero surrender charge from Year 7 onward enables continued participation in Option II’s variable account, where values depend on sub-account performance, reducing financial barriers to staying invested through market fluctuations.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables investment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges from Year 7 onward allows greater flexibility in accessing cash value, which complements the non-guaranteed nature of the death benefit under Option II by enabling investors to exit the policy without fees while accepting market-driven returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges from Year 7 onward supports longer retention of the policy, potentially enabling more strategic use of partial withdrawals without penalty, though such withdrawals still require a $1,000 minimum.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges from Year 7 onward allows greater flexibility in accessing funds, potentially enabling more frequent or larger partial withdrawals without penalty, though such withdrawals still reduce the face amount proportionally.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges from Year 7 onward supports sustained policy ownership, reducing the likelihood of premature termination and thereby helping prevent a lapse due to insufficient account value caused by excessive withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The lack of surrender charges after Year 7 allows investors greater flexibility to maintain or adjust investments, reducing pressure from premature withdrawals. This supports sustained funding, helping avoid lapses triggered by poor performance due to inadequate reserves.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">While premiums paid in Year 7 or later avoid surrender charges, partial withdrawals may still incur them, meaning the absence of premium-based charges does not eliminate withdrawal-related fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">partially contradicts</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99cfc4b3-4d83-4ce9-be87-237f5f1cfa94" target="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c">
