    <edge source="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">Lower charges characterize Option I, which also delivers a guaranteed level death benefit matching the face amount, enhancing its overall value proposition.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf" target="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2">
      <data key="d3">Lower charges in Option I likely reflect its lack of investment growth features, as minimal fees often accompany basic or non-variable options.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that Option I has lower charges than Option II, which directly supports Fact_sentence_2 by confirming the inverse relationship—that Option II incurs higher charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Option I’s lower charges make it more cost-efficient, which contrasts with Option II’s design allowing death benefit growth tied to investment performance, suggesting higher costs support its flexibility and upside.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">The lower charges of Option I make it more financially attractive, potentially influencing a policyholder’s choice to switch from Option II to Option I if cost efficiency is prioritized.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Option I’s lower charges suggest reduced financial burden, while Option II’s lack of guaranteed account value indicates exposure to market volatility. This implies that the cost savings in Option I may reflect a more stable, protected structure compared to the risky nature of Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a0af41ab-6fa6-4729-a72b-7004a7ef7560" target="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">reduced by</data>
