      <data key="d3">The absence of investment growth in Option I justifies its lower charging structure, aligning cost efficiency with restricted financial performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Option I lacks investment growth, making it fundamentally different from Option II, which allows the death benefit to vary based on account performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">Option I offers no investment growth, making it less dynamic compared to Option II, which carries higher fees despite potentially greater returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">comparative</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Option I provides no investment-based growth, contrasting sharply with Option II, where the death benefit increases alongside the account's performance due to exposure to market returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">no growth vs grows with account</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">Option I provides no investment growth, making it less attractive compared to Option II's potential for higher returns through market-linked gains. This limitation motivates the possibility of switching to Option II for better long-term outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Option I offers no investment growth, making it stable but without upside. In contrast, Option II allows fluctuating account values tied to market performance, introducing uncertainty.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Option I provides no investment growth, making it stable but limited in appreciation. In contrast, Option II's value varies according to sub-account performance, reflecting exposure to market gains or losses.</data>
      <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Option I provides no investment growth, making its death benefit predictable but unchanging. In contrast, Option II allows for fluctuating benefits based on market performance, meaning the death benefit is not guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">not guaranteed</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Option I provides no investment growth, making it fundamentally different from Option II, where the death benefit changes dynamically based on how well the underlying sub-accounts perform financially.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">Option I provides no investment growth, meaning its value remains static regardless of market conditions. This absence of growth contrasts with the Variable option, where gains or losses depend on market outcomes, placing full investment risk on the policyowner.</data>
      <data key="d4">no growth implies risk ownership</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Since Option I provides no investment growth, the account value remains stagnant, increasing the risk that it cannot sustain monthly charges over time, potentially resulting in policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
