    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">Sentence 2 specifies that the Variable option (Option II) is selected, meaning the stable, guaranteed benefit described in Sentence 1 does not govern the current policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">replaces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II is selected, the policyholder's death benefit becomes variable, tied to the account’s performance. This means the payout increases or decreases based on investment gains or losses.</data>
      <data key="d4">selected implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder's selection of Option II results in higher ongoing charges compared to Option I, reflecting the trade-off for potentially greater flexibility or investment control under the variable benefit structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyholder has chosen Option II, the death benefit is linked to the account's performance, meaning it increases when the account value rises.</data>
      <data key="d4">selects implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder currently uses the Variable death benefit option, which allows them to potentially increase benefits based on investment performance. This choice supports the possibility of switching to another option if desired.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="2248cf41-5aff-417f-8516-4b5df05a6c56">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II is currently selected, any attempt to change policies could trigger minimum face amount requirements, making the second fact relevant to potential transitions from the current state.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="7fbc30b8-9c5f-46d9-9b15-8aee78edbca2">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder has chosen the Variable death benefit option, which carries greater volatility. Switching from this option—even without changing the type—may necessitate proving insurability if coverage increases, reflecting regulatory safeguards around elevated risk exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyholder has chosen Option II, the account value fluctuates based on investment performance and carries inherent market risks, meaning it is not guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II implies that the death benefit is subject to market fluctuations and thus not guaranteed, reflecting its non-guaranteed nature tied to investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II is selected, the account value dynamically changes according to the performance of underlying sub-accounts, reflecting real-time market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyholder has chosen Option II, the death benefit becomes subject to changes based on the performance of underlying sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder’s choice of Option II (Variable) implies acceptance of investment risk, making it necessary for them to bear the full burden of potential losses or gains tied to market performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies risk</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II (Variable) is active, its performance directly affects the policy’s cash value. Poor investment returns under this option can deplete reserves, increasing the likelihood of policy lapse due to insufficient funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The selection of the Variable death benefit option exposes the policyholder to market risks, increasing the chance that the account value drops below required levels, potentially leading to policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II (Variable) is active, the policyholder is exposed to investment volatility. Other sub-accounts under this option do not guarantee any minimum return, increasing financial uncertainty tied to market performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="e908b03d-58ec-43af-9f19-e6a68cc15bb1">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder has chosen the Variable death benefit option, which includes access to sub-accounts such as the Money Market, where returns are subject to a guaranteed minimum interest rate of 1.5%. This ensures some baseline stability within the investment component.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II (Variable) establishes the context for applying the policy loan restriction, as it governs access to cash value through borrowing. This limitation ensures borrowers do not exceed sustainable withdrawal levels tied to the policy’s current financial standing.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II (Variable) is selected, any policy loan taken will directly reduce the death benefit on a one-to-one basis, reflecting the non-guaranteed nature of this benefit type.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="36ea11ef-2773-4656-b8f6-b515107b1be7">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder has chosen the Variable death benefit option, which allows flexibility in fund allocation. Loan disbursements under this option are directed into the Money Market sub-account, reflecting an administrative detail tied to the active choice of Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II (Variable) is active, the policyholder’s ability to make partial withdrawals is constrained by the current account value less $5,000, reflecting the variable nature of the underlying investments.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder has selected the Variable death benefit option, which influences how financial decisions like withdrawals impact the policy’s value over time. The $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals applies under this option, ensuring meaningful reductions only occur after substantial access to cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II establishes the policy's variable nature, under which partial withdrawals are governed by specific fees and reductions. The $50 processing fee applies whenever such withdrawals occur, making it a direct consequence of operating under this option.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II (Variable) is active, any partial withdrawal from the policy's accumulated value may incur surrender charges as outlined in Section 3.6, reflecting the financial impact of accessing funds under this flexible yet risky benefit choice.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies charges</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II (Variable Death Benefit) establishes the policy's dynamic nature, where changes like partial withdrawals directly influence the face amount based on underlying account value. This setting enables the rule in fact_sentence_2 to apply meaningfully.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">The confirmation that Option II is actively selected validates the earlier statement about its use, ensuring alignment with the described payout structure and financial implications.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">Since Option II is selected, the provision specifying that the death benefit equals the face amount plus account value becomes operationally relevant and enforceable.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms Option II is active, validating that the 0.90% M&amp;E charge mentioned in fact_sentence_1 is currently in effect.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad">
      <data key="d3">The ongoing daily deduction of the M&amp;E charge only applies because Option II has been selected, reinforcing its operational necessity within this plan type.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7" target="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df">
      <data key="d3">The allocation of premiums to sub-accounts after loading depends on Option II being active, making the policy's operational mechanics contingent on its current selection.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
