    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">Option II’s death benefit includes both the face amount and the account value, unlike Option I, which maintains a static benefit independent of investment gains.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2">
      <data key="d3">Option II includes a variable death benefit that depends on account value, contrasting sharply with Option I, which offers no such growth mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II determines that the death benefit includes both the guaranteed face amount and the current account value, reflecting its variable nature.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit in Option II depends on account performance, justifying the need for higher administrative or management charges compared to the guaranteed Level benefit in Option I.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II depends on the current account value, so when the account value rises, the total death benefit also increases accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a variable death benefit tied to account value in Option II enables meaningful differentiation from Option I, justifying the need for a switch mechanism between them.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit under Option II depends on an account value that is subject to market risks and thus not guaranteed, making its final payout uncertain.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II depends on the account value, which varies with investment performance, leading to an uncertain outcome. This variability means the benefit is not guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">not guaranteed</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II depends on the account value, which changes with investment returns. Therefore, its level fluctuates according to sub-account performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">drives</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II relies on the current account value, which is determined by the performance of underlying investments. This creates a direct link where fluctuations in the account value affect the total death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit depends on account performance, which introduces financial risk because the policyowner bears all investment risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit depends on account value, so declining account value from poor investments reduces financial cushion, increasing the chance of policy lapse if funds fall below required levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit depends on the account value, so if the account value declines too much, it could result in an inability to meet ongoing charges, leading to policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit under Option II relies on account value, which is influenced by sub-accounts without guaranteed returns, making the benefit subject to market risks beyond the Money Market sub-account.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit under Option II depends on the account value, so when a loan is taken, it reduces the available account value and thus lowers the overall death benefit accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
