    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">Higher charges associated with Option II justify why it was chosen over Option I only if the policyholder accepts elevated costs for potential upside, though this does not imply endorsement without consideration.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Higher charges in Option II reflect the added cost of managing variable investment components tied to fluctuating account values, which determine the total death benefit alongside the base face amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Higher charges in Option II reflect the increased investment flexibility and growth potential tied to account performance, enabling the death benefit to increase alongside the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">Option II carries higher fees compared to Option I, reflecting its greater expense profile. Despite this difference, policyholders retain the right to transition between the two options, allowing adaptability based on changing needs or market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Higher charges in Option II correlate with the elimination of a guaranteed death benefit, reflecting increased risk and variability tied to investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Higher charges in Option II increase pressure on the account's growth, reducing the likelihood of maintaining or increasing the account value over time, thereby contributing to its lack of guarantee.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Higher charges under Option II increase the risk of depleted account value over time, potentially leading to insufficient funds to meet ongoing costs and triggering a policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">Higher charges associated with Option II increase financial pressure on the policy, making it more vulnerable to lapse if investment performance declines.</data>
      <data key="d4">exacerbates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
