    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">The Variable option’s growing death benefit contrasts with the static nature of Option I’s level benefit, showing divergent design principles despite being part of the same policy type.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf">
      <data key="d3">The growth of the death benefit under Option II reflects its reliance on investment returns, implying higher operational or management costs, thus justifying why Option I has lower charges by comparison.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2">
      <data key="d3">Option II enables the death benefit to increase through favorable account performance, unlike Option I, which offers no such growth mechanism regardless of investment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">no growth vs grows with account</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit growing with the account value indicates that the policyholder has opted for the Variable option, which requires selection of Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies selection</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II is defined as the sum of the face amount and the account value, its growth is inherently tied to the performance of the account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit growing with the account value justifies the higher charges associated with Option II, as it reflects the risk and reward profile of investing in fluctuating markets.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">Option II’s death benefit rises with account value, reflecting its variable nature. This feature remains consistent regardless of whether the policyholder switches into or out of Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">The growth of the death benefit under Option II relies entirely on the account value, which is subject to market risks and thus not guaranteed. Without assurance of account value stability or increase, the promised growth cannot be reliably realized.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II increases with account performance, making it subject to market risks, which means it cannot be guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II increases when the account value rises, which depends on how well the underlying sub-accounts perform in the market.</data>
      <data key="d4">drives</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit increases when the account value rises, driven by favorable sub-account performance, leading to potential gains or losses depending on market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">The growth of the death benefit under Option II depends on investment returns, which are subject to market volatility. This variability exists because the policyowner assumes full responsibility for investment risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">Higher account performance boosts the death benefit under Option II, but weak returns diminish the policy's financial cushion, potentially leading to lapse if balances fall too low.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">When the account value rises under Option II, it helps maintain sufficient funds to meet ongoing charges, thereby reducing the likelihood of policy lapse due to insufficient balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d3">The growth of the Variable death benefit relies on investment performance across sub-accounts, many of which do not guarantee any minimum return, increasing volatility in benefit accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">The growth potential of the Variable death benefit depends on account performance, but any outstanding loans subtract directly from it, reducing its overall value regardless of gains.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">The growth potential of the Variable death benefit depends on the account’s performance, which influences available funds for withdrawals. Since partial withdrawals cannot exceed the account value minus $5,000, excessive withdrawals could limit future growth and thereby affect long-term death benefit accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes how the death benefit under Option II rises with account value, which directly supports and contextualizes why Option II was specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights that the death benefit under Option II grows with the account value, which directly supports and expands upon fact_sentence_1’s definition of the benefit formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">expands upon</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
