    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="09cdc94b-7cd3-44a1-8084-8305f1696fe3">
      <data key="d3">A higher account value driven by the growth of assets—including the 20% invested in government bonds—supports the escalating death benefit under Option II, making the asset mix relevant to its outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="711e0816-e0bc-445f-966b-4be7ac86e87f">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II grows with the account value, meaning any increase in the Money Market Fund’s contribution affects its long-term value and thus indirectly supports higher death benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit growing with account value means that the ongoing 0.90% mortality charge has a direct impact on its long-term increase by reducing accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf">
      <data key="d3">The growing death benefit under Option II depends on sustained account value growth, which is impacted by ongoing fees like the $15 monthly administrative charge described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d3">A rising death benefit under Option II implies increasing account value, which may raise the face amount at risk and consequently impact the Cost of Insurance as defined by the given formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="522644d7-e290-4908-b13c-663896d15b1c">
      <data key="d3">As the account value increases, the death benefit grows accordingly under Option II, which lowers the face amount at risk defined by the formula in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">A growing death benefit under Option II depends on strong account value appreciation, which is influenced by low expense ratios across sub-accounts, making the cost structure relevant to outcome viability.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">A growing death benefit tied to account value implies that fees like expense ratios (0.45%–1.25%) significantly influence long-term payout potential by affecting underlying investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on costs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce">
      <data key="d3">A higher-growing death benefit under Option II makes retaining the policy valuable, reinforcing the importance of minimizing early surrenders where high charges would erode those gains.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150" target="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c">
      <data key="d3">A rising death benefit tied to account value depends on uninterrupted investment growth, which is facilitated by no surrender charges after Year 7, allowing unhindered access to accumulated assets.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="377b464a-6e32-4a2d-b190-d24d4bdf4198" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">grows with account value</data>
    </edge>
