    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">The availability of switching options depends on having Option I defined, meaning its characteristics enable the broader functionality described in the second statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf">
      <data key="d3">Knowing that switches between options are permitted allows a policyholder to move toward Option I, which has lower charges, thereby optimizing long-term cost savings.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2">
      <data key="d3">The ability to switch between Option I and Option II enables policyholders to adapt their coverage strategy. Since Option I lacks growth potential, switching may be necessary to access greater benefit increases under favorable market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">Policyholders have the right to switch between Level and Variable death benefit options, meaning they could transition away from the currently selected Variable option under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">enabled by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">The availability of switching options allows policyholders to access or exit the variable benefit structure described in Fact Sentence 1 based on changing financial goals or market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">The availability of switching between Option I and Option II provides flexibility regardless of the associated costs. This choice capability exists independently of the specific charge levels, meaning the higher expenses of Option II remain unchanged even when switching occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Policyholders can choose to switch between Level and Variable options, enabling them to access the growth-linked death benefit described in Sentence 1 when selecting Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="2248cf41-5aff-417f-8516-4b5df05a6c56">
      <data key="d3">Switching between death benefit options requires meeting minimum face amount thresholds, ensuring policyholders maintain sufficient coverage levels during transitions.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="831aae49-4936-4c7a-b432-1eb7b1154300">
      <data key="d3">Switching between death benefit options triggers an administrative fee, reflecting operational costs tied to modifying policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="7fbc30b8-9c5f-46d9-9b15-8aee78edbca2">
      <data key="d3">Switching between death benefit options allows flexibility, but if the change results in higher coverage, the insurer mandates proof of insurability to mitigate risk exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">requires condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Switching to Option II exposes the policyholder to non-guaranteed account values tied to market performance, meaning the account’s worth fluctuates without assurance.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Switching to Option II exposes the policyholder to non-guaranteed death benefits, as this option's payout depends on investment performance and carries market risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Switching to Option II grants the policyholder access to an account whose value changes according to underlying sub-account investments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Switching to Option II allows the policyholder to access a death benefit tied to sub-account performance, meaning gains or losses in investments affect the payout. This variability makes understanding Option II’s behavior essential when considering a switch.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Switching between death benefit options might affect the account's financial stability, potentially influencing whether it remains sufficient to meet ongoing charges and prevent lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
