      <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required when increasing coverage during a switch between death benefit options. This requirement applies regardless of whether the current choice is the Variable option, ensuring financial stability and risk control across transitions.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7fbc30b8-9c5f-46d9-9b15-8aee78edbca2" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is necessary before switching to ensure the policyholder remains eligible for increased coverage, reinforcing the need for underwriting validation during transitions.</data>
      <data key="d4">condition for switching</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7fbc30b8-9c5f-46d9-9b15-8aee78edbca2" target="2248cf41-5aff-417f-8516-4b5df05a6c56">
      <data key="d3">Switching options necessitates meeting minimum face amount thresholds, which may prompt the requirement for proof of insurability if coverage increases beyond those limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7fbc30b8-9c5f-46d9-9b15-8aee78edbca2" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Switching to higher coverage under Option II requires proof of insurability due to its non-guaranteed death benefit, reflecting increased risk exposure from market volatility.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7fbc30b8-9c5f-46d9-9b15-8aee78edbca2" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Changing from one death benefit option to another, especially if increasing coverage, necessitates proof of insurability. This requirement applies within the framework where Option II's account value lacks guarantees due to market volatility.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual relation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
