    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="d718d2dd-4dc4-4503-a75d-71ee2866b3bf">
      <data key="d3">The non-guaranteed account value under Option II reflects inherent investment risk, which justifies why it might have higher charges than Option I. Therefore, the lack of guarantee supports the notion that Option II carries added expense or risk relative to Option I.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2">
      <data key="d3">The lack of guaranteed account value in Option II reflects its reliance on volatile markets, while Option I avoids such risks by offering no growth potential.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II implies exposure to market-driven variability, making the account value non-guaranteed, consistent with the stated condition.</data>
      <data key="d4">implied by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Since the account value under Option II is not guaranteed, any death benefit tied to it—including the one defined by combining face amount and account value—is inherently unstable and exposed to financial volatility.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a guaranteed account value under Option II reflects inherent instability tied to market risks, which justifies the imposition of higher charges to offset insurer risk and administrative costs.</data>
      <data key="d4">justified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Since the account value under Option II is not guaranteed, any expectation of increasing death benefits tied to its performance becomes uncertain and contingent on unpredictable market outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a guaranteed account value under Option II justifies why such an option requires careful consideration when deciding whether to switch from Option I.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="7fbc30b8-9c5f-46d9-9b15-8aee78edbca2">
      <data key="d3">The lack of guarantee on the account value under Option II reflects its exposure to market risk. This characteristic influences decisions involving coverage adjustments, requiring proof of insurability when upgrading.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">The account value under Option II lacks guarantees because its performance depends entirely on the underlying sub-accounts' returns, leading to potential gains or losses.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">The account value under Option II fluctuates based on market conditions, meaning its uncertainty directly impacts the final death benefit, which also varies accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
