    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">Option II’s death benefit changes according to investment results, unlike Option I, which maintains a fixed payout independent of market activity.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2">
      <data key="d3">Option II features variable death benefits driven by investment results, unlike Option I, which explicitly prohibits any growth from investments.</data>
      <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The fluctuation of the death benefit under Option II indicates that the policyholder has opted into a variable benefit structure, consistent with choosing Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit includes the account value, any change in sub-account performance affects the total benefit, making it dependent on those investments.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Fluctuations in the death benefit occur because it is tied directly to changes in sub-account performance, which determines how much the account value—and thus the benefit—grows or declines.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">Option II’s variable death benefit depends on investment outcomes, making its use potentially advantageous or risky compared to Option I. Therefore, the possibility of switching enables the policyholder to align coverage with their risk tolerance and financial goals.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="2248cf41-5aff-417f-8516-4b5df05a6c56">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of Option II’s death benefit depends on investment outcomes, which influences whether switching into it meets regulatory or policyholder eligibility criteria like minimum face amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II adjusts according to sub-account performance, this inherent volatility inherently makes the underlying account value non-guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II fluctuates with sub-account performance, it cannot be guaranteed, making future payouts uncertain.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II adjusts with sub-account performance, it reflects changes in the underlying account value driven by those same investment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">depended on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">The fluctuation in the death benefit under Option II results from the policyowner assuming full investment risk, meaning gains or losses in sub-accounts directly affect the payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Poor sub-account performance reduces the account value, increasing the risk that it falls below the level needed to cover ongoing costs, potentially causing the policy to lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The variability of the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account returns, so when those returns are negative or poor, the policy’s cash value diminishes, increasing the risk of lapse if reserves fall below required levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">The Variable death benefit increases or decreases with sub-account returns, and any policy loan directly subtracts from this dynamic benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d3">The variation in the death benefit under Option II stems from the performance of sub-accounts, particularly those without guaranteed returns like the Money Market sub-account.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">The variability of the death benefit under Option II depends on investment returns, which influences the total account value from which partial withdrawals are limited. This means withdrawal limits are tied to the current state of the variable component.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II implies a flexible death benefit that adjusts according to sub-account performance, aligning with the described volatility in payouts.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option II depends on both the guaranteed face amount and the volatile account value, meaning it can vary based on investment outcomes linked to sub-account performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains mechanism</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II rises or falls with sub-account performance, it interacts with the fixed 0.90% M&amp;E charge, which continuously reduces the account balance and thus affects long-term benefit accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II changes with investment returns, the ongoing daily deduction of the M&amp;E charge diminishes the account’s growth potential, affecting the final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df">
      <data key="d3">The variation in the death benefit under Option II depends on the performance of sub-accounts, which are funded by premiums after deduction of the premium load.</data>
      <data key="d4">driven by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of the death benefit under Option II depends on the performance of sub-accounts, which are funded by ongoing premium allocations described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of the death benefit relies on sub-account returns, which are shaped by how investors allocate premiums—a process governed by the rules outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281">
      <data key="d3">The fluctuating nature of the death benefit under Option II depends on the performance of sub-accounts like the Equity Growth Fund, making it contingent on its investment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="c6b46ac7-78f4-449c-8b45-6fd65adfbba6">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account returns—including the Balanced Allocation Fund—the presence and behavior of this fund directly impact the potential growth and volatility of the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="0ec4db95-1572-487f-90d2-c5a822614352">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account performance, making the existence and role of the Government Bond Fund relevant to understanding how benefits may change over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="a6548f00-c863-44e8-a21a-b412497ba0bc">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account performance, the existence and role of the Money Market Fund—as an active component of those investments—is relevant to understanding how the benefit can vary over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="c2037215-53c9-4630-94af-e8bb4930956c">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account returns, the presence of the Real Estate Securities Fund influences its performance and thus affects the fluctuating death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="5471d238-37e9-4478-8504-a41c8fe37a7b">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of the death benefit under Option II means that shifts in the Equity Growth Fund's performance—which is currently set at 40% of assets—can influence the ultimate payout, making the allocation level relevant to expected outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="3014df8f-db7d-4af8-9b3e-fa9f179736e5">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II varies with sub-account performance, the specific allocation of 30% to the Balanced Allocation Fund plays a role in determining the magnitude and direction of those fluctuations.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="09cdc94b-7cd3-44a1-8084-8305f1696fe3">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II fluctuates with sub-account performance, the specific allocation to the Government Bond Fund (20%) plays a role in determining those performance outcomes, making the funding mix relevant to the benefit’s variability.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="711e0816-e0bc-445f-966b-4be7ac86e87f">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of the death benefit depends on sub-account returns, so the specific allocation to the Money Market Fund impacts long-term growth and thus the final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account returns, meaning the impact of the 0.90% annual charge accumulates within those investments, shaping long-term benefit levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf">
      <data key="d3">The variable death benefit tied to sub-account performance depends on underlying investments funded by premium allocations, which are subject to an ongoing $15 monthly administrative fee.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d3">A rising death benefit under Option II reflects improved sub-account performance, which may expand the face amount at risk and consequently raise the Cost of Insurance as per the given formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="522644d7-e290-4908-b13c-663896d15b1c">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II varies with sub-account returns, its level relative to the account value continuously shifts, thereby changing the face amount at risk—the difference between the two—which governs key expenses like the variable cost-of-insurance.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account performance, differences in individual sub-account expense ratios can alter long-term growth and thus impact the final benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">Since the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account performance, the associated expense ratios (0.45%–1.25%) play a direct role in determining how much value accumulates within those accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce">
      <data key="d3">A higher-performing sub-account increases the death benefit under Option II, making it more valuable to hold the policy longer to avoid high initial surrender charges.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2">
      <data key="d3">Variable death benefits depend on sub-account returns, so policies subject to high surrender charges may discourage premature exits, preserving potential gains linked to those accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130">
      <data key="d3">The variability of the death benefit under Option II means its final payout depends heavily on investment outcomes in sub-accounts, which indirectly influences the impact of a 5% surrender charge when withdrawing early, especially if those investments have not grown sufficiently.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476">
      <data key="d3">The variability of the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account returns, making early surrenders subject to a 3% charge more consequential, as poor-performing assets could lead to reduced payouts despite fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7" target="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c">
      <data key="d3">The variable nature of the death benefit under Option II depends on sub-account returns, making timely premium payment and retention crucial; avoiding surrender charges past Year 7 preserves capital needed to support higher potential payouts.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b34b4332-4e76-4380-aea9-fd454e54adc9" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on sub account performance</data>
    </edge>
