    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyowner bears full investment risk, the existence of a level death benefit ensures protection against such volatility through guaranteed payouts.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="ff1a79b3-08d5-49d1-a8e3-3b8a90ed15c2">
      <data key="d3">The policyowner bears all investment risk under the Variable option, reflecting that returns are uncertain and tied to market performance. In contrast, Option I avoids such risks altogether by offering no opportunity for investment-based growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">no growth implies risk ownership</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">Because the policyholder bears all investment risk, selecting Option II ensures alignment with the inherent volatility of the Variable death benefit, reflecting ownership responsibility over financial outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">required by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyowner assumes full investment risk, the resulting variability in account value directly affects the calculation of the variable death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyowner bears all investment risk, changes in the account’s value directly impact the death benefit under Option II, leading to potential increases or decreases over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Because the policyowner bears all investment risk, it follows that the account value under Option II cannot be guaranteed, reflecting the inherent uncertainty of market-driven returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyowner bears all investment risk, it follows that the death benefit under Option II cannot be guaranteed, as outcomes depend on unpredictable market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyholder bears full investment risk, the account value naturally varies according to sub-account performance, reflecting real-time market impacts.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Because the policyowner bears all investment risk, the death benefit under Option II naturally varies depending on the performance of underlying sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy owner bears all investment risk, negative returns on investments can deplete the cash value, potentially leading to insufficient funds to maintain coverage and resulting in policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy owner bears all investment risk, declines in account value due to market conditions can result in insufficient funds to meet ongoing charges, potentially causing the policy to lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d3">The policyholder bears full investment risk, which includes exposure to potential losses in sub-accounts without guaranteed returns beyond the Money Market option.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="e908b03d-58ec-43af-9f19-e6a68cc15bb1">
      <data key="d3">The policy owner bears full investment risk, yet the Money Market sub-account offers a safety net through a guaranteed minimum interest rate of 1.5%, reducing potential losses during downturns.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">Since the policyowner bears all investment risk, any use of policy value through loans directly diminishes the available death benefit, aligning financial exposure with control over assets.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The policy owner bears full investment risk, meaning any reduction in policy value from partial withdrawals reflects their personal financial decisions and exposure to market volatility. This justifies the proportional decrease in the face amount when withdrawals occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">The policy owner bears full investment risk, meaning any decline in account value affects available funds for withdrawals. This risk context justifies the $5,000 buffer in the partial withdrawal rule, ensuring some capital remains protected.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The ownership of investment risk implies that policyholders bear losses from poor market performance, which indirectly influences how much value remains available for withdrawals. This context makes it relevant that partial withdrawals may incur surrender charges if not managed carefully.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="310733ee-587a-4403-9f44-61c184d1f774" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
