    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">If poor investment performance lowers the account value, it diminishes the total death benefit under Option II, potentially leading to inadequate reserves to maintain coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="aa2bafea-758d-4319-863f-08d9cd460b15">
      <data key="d3">The risk of policy lapse from poor investment performance underscores why Option II's higher charges are particularly consequential for long-term sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d4">amplified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">If investment performance declines significantly, the reduced account value undermines the policy’s sustainability, making it harder to maintain coverage despite the potential for higher death benefits tied to strong performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">A policy may lapse due to poor investment returns because the account value under Option II is not guaranteed, making it susceptible to declines caused by adverse market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">If poor investment performance occurs, the policy’s cash value may decline significantly, leading to potential lapse—a direct outcome of the non-guaranteed nature of the death benefit described in Sentence 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">If the policy faces inadequate funding due to poor investment returns, it risks lapsing, which stems directly from the variable nature of the account value outlined in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">If the policy experiences poor investment performance, the resulting decline in value reduces the ability to sustain premiums, potentially leading to a lapse, which undermines the foundation of the variable death benefit feature.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of policy lapse due to poor investment performance arises directly from the fact that the policy owner assumes full responsibility for investment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Poor investment performance reduces the account value, potentially leading to insufficient funds to meet monthly deductions, which triggers policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="e908b03d-58ec-43af-9f19-e6a68cc15bb1">
      <data key="d3">Poor investment performance increases the risk of policy lapse due to declining cash value, though the guaranteed 1.5% minimum on the Money Market sub-account offers some protection against total collapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d3">If investments underperform in non-guaranteed sub-accounts, the policy’s cash value may decline, increasing the risk of lapse due to inadequate funding. Since only the Money Market sub-account has a guaranteed return, exposure to volatile options heightens financial instability.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43">
      <data key="d3">If investment performance declines, the policy's cash value diminishes, reducing its ability to support premium payments. This increases reliance on loans, whose limits (capped at 90% of surrender value) constrain available liquidity during downturns.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">If investment returns decline significantly, the account value drops, potentially reducing the buffer that allows safe partial withdrawals. This makes it harder to maintain sufficient reserves, increasing the risk of lapse if withdrawals exceed sustainable levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">If investment returns underperform, the policy’s cash value may drop significantly, potentially leading to a need for loans to maintain coverage. Each such loan directly reduces the death benefit, exacerbating the financial strain caused by weak performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">exacerbates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">Poor investment performance reduces the policy’s cash value, increasing the likelihood of insufficient funds. This makes partial withdrawals more risky, especially if surrender charges further diminish available reserves.</data>
      <data key="d4">exacerbates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient investment results in low cash value, making it harder to sustain premium payments and increasing the likelihood of policy lapse despite proper allocation mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5">
      <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to poor performance, it reflects inadequate results from the sub-account allocations made per the investor’s instructions, underscoring the importance of strategic distribution.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281">
      <data key="d3">If the Equity Growth Fund underperforms, it increases the risk of policy lapse, making its performance a key factor in maintaining policy validity despite stable premium allocations.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="c6b46ac7-78f4-449c-8b45-6fd65adfbba6">
      <data key="d3">Poor investment performance across sub-accounts like the Balanced Allocation Fund reduces the policy's cash value, undermining its ability to sustain premium payments and fees, thereby threatening the policy’s continuation and risking lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="0ec4db95-1572-487f-90d2-c5a822614352">
      <data key="d3">Poor investment performance, such as that affecting the Government Bond Fund, reduces the policy's cash value, increasing the risk of lapse due to inadequate funding to sustain premium obligations and fees.</data>
