      <data key="d3">If the policy faces poor investment outcomes—such as those stemming from underperforming equity investments—the resulting decline in account value increases the risk of lapse, making the current 40% allocation to the Equity Growth Fund a contributing factor.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="3014df8f-db7d-4af8-9b3e-fa9f179736e5">
      <data key="d3">If the policy faces poor investment performance, particularly within key sub-accounts such as the Balanced Allocation Fund (currently holding 30%), it may deplete reserves enough to cause the policy to lapse despite its existing allocation structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
