      <data key="d3">Poor investment performance diminishes the account value, making it harder to cover recurring fees like the 0.90% mortality charge, potentially leading to insufficient funds and policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">increased vulnerability</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf">
      <data key="d3">Poor investment performance diminishes available cash value, making it harder to cover mandatory expenses like the $15 monthly administrative fee, thereby increasing the chance of policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases exposure</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d3">If poor investment results cause the policy’s cash value to decline, it becomes harder to pay the COI, which is determined by the face amount at risk and the monthly rate—making continued coverage unsustainable.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="522644d7-e290-4908-b13c-663896d15b1c">
      <data key="d3">If poor investment returns erode the account value, the resulting increase in face amount at risk raises the cost of insurance and threatens solvency, making it harder to maintain sufficient funds to prevent policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">If a policy's investments perform poorly, low cash values may not cover ongoing expenses like those tied to sub-accounts, making high expense ratios more likely to push the policy toward lapse despite flexible allocation options.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to poor performance, it suggests underlying issues such as excessive fees like those in the 0.45%–1.25% expense ratio range, which erode capital and hinder recovery.</data>
