      <data key="d3">Poor investment outcomes threaten policy survival through potential lapse, making upfront surrender charges more consequential—they restrict options to stabilize the policy’s value during downturns.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f" target="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130">
      <data key="d3">If poor investment results threaten policy lapse, the 5% surrender charge in Years 3–4 limits viable recovery options by penalizing withdrawals, worsening financial strain.</data>
