      <data key="d3">If the account value declines too much, leading to potential lapses, it indicates that the growth mechanism tied to the account value (as per Option II) has failed to keep pace with expenses.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55" target="6e4a5644-f48d-427f-ba8d-2997378c8b42">
      <data key="d3">Insufficient account value risking policy lapse underscores why managing benefit options carefully—including the possibility of switching—is important for maintaining coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
