    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The absence of guaranteed minimum returns in most sub-accounts aligns with the nature of the Variable option, which is currently chosen. Thus, the selection of Option II logically implies acceptance of such return variability.</data>
      <data key="d4">implied by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Since other sub-accounts offer no guaranteed minimum return, changes in their performance affect the account value, thereby impacting the total death benefit defined in Option II.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Because the Variable death benefit rises with account value, its stability and predictability depend heavily on whether underlying investments offer guaranteed returns—a feature absent in most sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that among sub-accounts, only the Money Market one has a guaranteed return, reinforcing why the total account value under Option II cannot be guaranteed, thus supporting fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Since other sub-accounts have no guaranteed returns, it reinforces why the death benefit under Option II cannot be guaranteed, as its value depends on volatile investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Since other sub-accounts lack guaranteed returns, their performance directly influences the volatility of the account value, leading to unpredictable changes in the overall account balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Sub-accounts excluding the Money Market offer no guaranteed returns, contributing to the non-guaranteed fluctuations seen in the Variable death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">Since other sub-accounts offer no guaranteed minimum return, the policyholder assumes greater financial risk, consistent with bearing investment risk entirely.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The absence of guaranteed returns in most sub-accounts means investment losses are possible, which could deplete the policy's value and lead to lapse if not managed properly.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The lack of guaranteed returns in most sub-accounts introduces volatility that can lead to declining account values, increasing the likelihood of policy lapse when fees exceed available balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="e908b03d-58ec-43af-9f19-e6a68cc15bb1">
      <data key="d3">While most sub-accounts offer no guaranteed returns, the Money Market sub-account stands out by providing a 1.5% guaranteed minimum interest rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">has guarantee</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="36ea11ef-2773-4656-b8f6-b515107b1be7">
      <data key="d3">Since other sub-accounts offer no guaranteed returns, transferring loan amounts into the Money Market sub-account ensures stability and predictability for the borrowed funds, minimizing exposure to volatility.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances stability</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">The absence of guaranteed returns in most sub-accounts introduces uncertainty in account value, which indirectly affects how much can be withdrawn via partial withdrawals. This variability influences the cap defined by subtracting $5,000 from the current account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ae26d7c2-3735-4369-afdb-7630db653d1a" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">no guaranteed return elsewhere</data>
    </edge>
