    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The 90% cap on policy loans reflects a safeguard designed specifically for policies like Option II, where fluctuating account values necessitate controlled borrowing limits based on real-time surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrained by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Loan restrictions limiting borrowing to 90% of surrender value serve as a safeguard against excessive depletion of assets, especially important given that the Variable death benefit lacks guarantees and depends on investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">supports context</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans cannot exceed 90% of the surrender value, meaning that changes in the account’s performance—which affect surrender value—directly constrain the available loan size.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The 90% ceiling on policy loans restricts access to cash value, limiting the policyholder’s ability to offset losses from poor investments. Without sufficient funds, the policy risks lapsing when contributions fall short.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans are restricted to 90% of the surrender value, limiting how much cash can be withdrawn. Excessive borrowing reduces available account value, increasing the chance of insufficient funds leading to policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="f1fab3de-ee39-499b-b5bb-1d9134b0517d">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes the cap on how much can be borrowed via policy loan, while fact sentence 2 clarifies the financial cost associated with such borrowing by specifying the fixed annual interest rate.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="36ea11ef-2773-4656-b8f6-b515107b1be7">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan is capped at 90% of the surrender value, and any such loaned amount is directed into the Money Market sub-account as part of the policy’s investment framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan is capped at 90% of the surrender value, which ensures that any borrowed amount cannot exceed this threshold. Each such loan directly diminishes the death benefit by the same dollar amount, maintaining proportional impact.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c810f004-b8ef-41e7-9db0-f1674c47c3bb" target="6609aab0-8bef-493f-a6c7-30042cfc3b43">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
    </edge>
