    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="979657f2-f415-4532-85c2-c22846a07e62">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">withdrawal</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="ca3b25f7-b1c2-42c4-9b74-d463a7ccb905">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">fee</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="e601060b-82bb-4d4d-bf85-08135fb0f2fb">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">charge</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="0f918cc3-1469-461d-8506-b7f6189e70ce">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">reduction</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">A mandatory $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals ensures significant changes to the policy's cash value, particularly relevant when the Variable option is active, since those withdrawals directly reduce the face amount based on proportional reduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">The requirement of a $1,000 minimum ensures withdrawals are meaningful, while being limited to the account value minus $5,000 prevents excessive depletion of reserves needed for policy stability.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The $1,000 minimum withdrawal amount sets a baseline condition that triggers the application of the $50 processing fee, ensuring only meaningful withdrawals incur administrative costs.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions fee</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The $1,000 minimum withdrawal requirement sets a baseline for initiating a transaction that could trigger applicable surrender charges under Section 3.6.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">A minimum withdrawal of $1,000 triggers the mechanism that reduces the policy's face amount proportionally. This ensures only meaningful withdrawals impact the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals under the policy, subject to a $1,000 minimum, impact the death benefit defined under Option II by lowering it accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals decrease the face amount, thereby affecting the total death benefit calculated as face amount plus account value, as specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals exceeding $1,000 reduce the total account balance, thereby affecting the amount eligible for future premium allocation into sub-accounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces available funds</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5">
      <data key="d3">A minimum $1,000 partial withdrawal requirement implies investors must have adequate balances in their sub-accounts, reinforcing the importance of proper allocation decisions guided by investment instructions.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281">
      <data key="d3">The $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals impacts access to funds held in the Equity Growth Fund, limiting when and how much an investor can withdraw from this sub-account.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences access</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="c6b46ac7-78f4-449c-8b45-6fd65adfbba6">
      <data key="d3">A required $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals implies that investors need substantial accumulated value, likely derived from allocations—including those into the Balanced Allocation Fund—to qualify.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables conditional access</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="0ec4db95-1572-487f-90d2-c5a822614352">
      <data key="d3">The $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals applies across all sub-accounts, including the Government Bond Fund, ensuring consistent liquidity controls regardless of underlying asset type.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="a6548f00-c863-44e8-a21a-b412497ba0bc">
      <data key="d3">The $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals implies that investors need sufficient accumulated value across all sub-accounts—including the Money Market Fund—to qualify, making the existence of this fund relevant to meeting withdrawal thresholds.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="c2037215-53c9-4630-94af-e8bb4930956c">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals requiring a $1,000 minimum apply to the entire investment portfolio, including assets held in the Real Estate Securities Fund, meaning distributions from this fund would need to meet the same threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="3014df8f-db7d-4af8-9b3e-fa9f179736e5">
      <data key="d3">A $1,000 minimum partial withdrawal impacts the overall balance of the Balanced Allocation Fund, especially since it holds 30% of total assets, thereby indirectly influencing its future performance and rebalancing dynamics.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33">
      <data key="d3">A $1,000 minimum partial withdrawal requirement affects cash access, meaning only substantial withdrawals impact the account value used to calculate the 0.90% annual mortality charge, linking usage patterns to cost exposure.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences cost structure</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d3">A reduction in the face amount from partial withdrawals lowers the face amount at risk, thereby reducing the cost of insurance under the given formula, linking withdrawal behavior to ongoing premium expenses.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="522644d7-e290-4908-b13c-663896d15b1c">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reduce the face amount at risk because they decrease the death benefit, making the concept from fact_sentence_1 more relevant during such transactions.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">A $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals means investors must ensure sufficient accumulated value after accounting for expense ratios, which erode gains over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals require a $1,000 minimum and incur fees, which may intersect with surrender charges when large withdrawals occur near the end of the surrender period.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="5d223ba0-ac0f-4dce-85c5-d0617f2418c2">
      <data key="d3">A minimum $1,000 threshold for partial withdrawals ensures meaningful transactions, while the 7% surrender charge in initial years penalizes complete policy cancellations—both mechanisms regulate access to accumulated value under distinct conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">supplements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="69608bdc-7106-4794-a6fc-06a70dd54130">
      <data key="d3">A mandatory $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals could lead investors to avoid frequent small withdrawals, thereby reducing exposure to potential surrender charges tied to premature policy termination under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">considered in</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="20ce4777-7e1a-4273-b5c7-82e39fac1476">
      <data key="d3">A minimum $1,000 threshold for partial withdrawals complements the timing-based surrender charge by defining limits on fund access, ensuring that only meaningful withdrawals occur even when fees apply.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e" target="8fec2bf4-e22f-45fa-a2fe-5c9e5a9f591c">
      <data key="d3">A $1,000 minimum for partial withdrawals aligns with policies designed to discourage frequent small withdrawals, especially when combined with no surrender charges post-Year 7, suggesting an emphasis on sustained investment rather than short-term cash access.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4f8761f8-f60b-4cb1-b285-e70db0a36f6d" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to minimum partial withdrawal amount</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="979657f2-f415-4532-85c2-c22846a07e62" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">requires minimum withdrawal amount of 1000</data>
    </edge>
