    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Option II restricts partial withdrawals to an amount not exceeding the account value minus $5,000, ensuring alignment with the policy’s variable benefit framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals cannot exceed the account value minus $5,000, this cap constrains how much of the account value contributing to the death benefit can be accessed without affecting future benefit levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="fa381acf-443b-4930-8921-e02cc04b1150">
      <data key="d3">Limitations on partial withdrawals—capped at the account value minus $5,000—are designed to preserve sufficient capital within the account to support ongoing growth, which directly supports the increasing nature of the Variable death benefit over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="74e421cc-1b7d-4755-b72f-7b9f5f6bbfe9">
      <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals cannot exceed the account value minus $5,000, the unguaranteed nature of the account value under Option II ensures that withdrawal limits remain dynamic and subject to market changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Limitations on partial withdrawals—capped at account value minus $5,000—are designed to preserve sufficient reserves, especially important given that the death benefit under Option II is not guaranteed and thus vulnerable to erosion from excessive withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals are limited by the current account value less $5,000, the potential for such withdrawals hinges entirely on how well the underlying investments perform over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="b84d9a61-e856-449c-a1b7-ffd3b834c5a7">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals cannot exceed the account value minus $5,000, meaning the maximum allowable withdrawal is constrained by the net asset base supporting the variable death benefit, thus affecting its potential volatility over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrained by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">The restriction limiting partial withdrawals to the account value minus $5,000 helps preserve residual assets, reinforcing the idea that the policy owner assumes complete responsibility for investment outcomes and potential losses.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="1d7528cf-578b-4c9e-805a-b6d7077a310f">
      <data key="d3">The cap on partial withdrawals ensures some reserve remains in the account after each withdrawal, helping preserve capital needed to avoid lapses during periods of poor performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal depends on having enough account value after retaining a buffer of $5,000, ensuring that remaining funds can still support ongoing charges and prevent lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="23382f49-1a75-4d65-9ae8-9d92f5aabd4c">
      <data key="d3">The rule limiting partial withdrawals to the account value minus $5,000 ensures that sufficient reserves remain even if sub-accounts fluctuate without guaranteed returns, protecting against depletion during volatile periods.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrained by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">Withdrawals cannot exceed the account value after retaining $5,000, ensuring sufficient cushion remains, and must also meet or surpass the $1,000 floor to qualify.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal is limited to the account value minus $5,000. This restriction governs how much can be withdrawn, regardless of fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="0f79fac3-4cc7-4db8-9988-95a22ef09fff">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal is limited by the account value minus $5,000, and this withdrawal may be subject to surrender charges if specified in section 3.6.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450" target="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal is limited to the account value minus $5,000, ensuring a buffer remains in the policy. This restriction supports the rule that any withdrawal reduces the face amount proportionally by maintaining financial integrity.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6d4cce97-705f-4671-bbb3-faaa6062211a" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
