    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="decd6c86-36db-45ea-88cb-14b69bb2fa9f">
      <data key="d3">Since Option I guarantees a level death benefit based on the face amount, any reduction in that face amount via partial withdrawals diminishes the final death benefit accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="0a3e0c50-8fc9-4679-94bb-856bff774ce7">
      <data key="d3">Because partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally under the current policy setup, selecting Option II ensures such adjustments reflect real-time account performance and maintain alignment with the variable benefit structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="63433ceb-81a0-44ea-95a1-c6bc9c2ae0de">
      <data key="d3">Reducing the face amount through partial withdrawals affects the total death benefit because the benefit includes both the face amount and the account value, meaning any change to the former alters the final payout outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="d7bbd6d3-1f46-4341-bd8b-0214db62b50d">
      <data key="d3">Reducing the face amount through partial withdrawals impacts the death benefit, which is already non-guaranteed under Option II. This action reinforces the absence of a stable or protected payout level.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="fc50e6da-a35a-4b0b-b4b6-a838415c3d5c">
      <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally, the resulting reduction impacts the overall account value, reflecting the financial consequences of such actions within the variable component of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="c77d0c8c-e192-4a05-988c-04e682d69d67">
      <data key="d3">When partial withdrawals are made, the face amount decreases proportionally because the policyowner assumes all investment risk—their own actions and market outcomes directly affect the policy’s value and coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Reducing the face amount through partial withdrawals diminishes the policy’s cash value buffer, making it more vulnerable to falling below the threshold needed to meet ongoing charges, thereby raising the risk of policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="280ab5d3-6e4f-4198-81c8-a2ef27b919d6">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals decrease the face amount in direct proportion to the withdrawn sum, thereby reducing future death benefits without affecting the loan balance or interest obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="67ae83fb-0cf5-44ec-b533-6271ab72c41e">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to withdraw at least $1,000 exists so that any reduction in the face amount remains significant and aligned with policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">enforces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="29d195f0-f43e-425b-a095-af01a0765450">
      <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally, the policy enforces a cap of the account value minus $5,000 to prevent excessive depletion and maintain solvency.</data>
      <data key="d4">enforces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="dc514d96-9b2a-40a5-941c-7335baaddd7f">
      <data key="d3">When a partial withdrawal is made, the policy’s face amount decreases proportionally to reflect the reduced cash value. This action triggers a mandatory $50 processing fee regardless of the withdrawal size.</data>
      <data key="d4">incurred by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="3ee62998-6a05-40f4-921c-b0c4be892b48">
      <data key="d3">The rule that partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally is integral to maintaining the integrity of Option II’s death benefit calculation, where payouts depend on both base face value and account accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="67add080-3372-4301-bd74-0e6a0c67fa5b">
      <data key="d3">The rule that the death benefit equals Face Amount plus Account Value under Option II means any reduction in face amount due to withdrawals directly lowers the overall death benefit payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="15d5a489-4261-4d61-bf32-69164a87bed6">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally affect the underlying account balance subject to the 0.90% M&amp;E charge, thereby influencing ongoing cost calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="2ac01dcd-f72c-441c-8596-afeaf23404ad">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals directly reduce the face amount proportionally, meaning that the effect of the daily M&amp;E charge becomes increasingly significant over time because less capital remains to absorb those costs, potentially accelerating depletion of the policy's value.</data>
      <data key="d4">amplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="1ea37a9c-a314-44d4-942c-f27d3a8728df">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals decrease the face amount based on current account value, affecting how future premiums contribute to growing the policy's overall worth.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="c7801d49-390a-4eb6-a6cc-c11043c369ef">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally, impacting the policy's value and indirectly constraining future premium allocation effectiveness by reducing the funded base.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects allocation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="1dbe7802-6ae3-4a4f-a1b6-0103ad7965b5">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally rely on the existing distribution of assets across sub-accounts, meaning the initial allocation process described in fact_sentence_1 influences the outcome of such withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="de269cdd-b80a-4bb9-adc9-121b0cf85281">
      <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally, investing in the Equity Growth Fund could influence the extent of such reductions when withdrawals occur, given its role in the portfolio mix.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="c6b46ac7-78f4-449c-8b45-6fd65adfbba6">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally depend on the underlying sub-account structure, such as the Balanced Allocation Fund, which determines how assets are managed during these transactions.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="0ec4db95-1572-487f-90d2-c5a822614352">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally depend on underlying asset allocations such as the Government Bond Fund, shaping how policyholder liquidity events alter financial guarantees.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="a6548f00-c863-44e8-a21a-b412497ba0bc">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally affect the valuation of sub-account balances like the Money Market Fund by lowering the total policy value upon which those assets contribute.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="c2037215-53c9-4630-94af-e8bb4930956c">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally depend on the underlying asset composition—including exposure to funds such as the Real Estate Securities Fund—which shapes the account’s value and thus determines the extent of reductions during withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="5471d238-37e9-4478-8504-a41c8fe37a7b">
      <data key="d3">Reduced face amounts resulting from partial withdrawals indirectly reflect shifts in effective portfolio exposure, potentially altering future allocation dynamics even though the stated 40% remains unchanged until rebalancing occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="3014df8f-db7d-4af8-9b3e-fa9f179736e5">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally depend on the underlying asset composition—including the 30% held in the Balanced Allocation Fund—that determines the policy’s cash value and eligibility for such distributions.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="09cdc94b-7cd3-44a1-8084-8305f1696fe3">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally depend on the current distribution of assets, such as the 20% held in the Government Bond Fund, affecting the valuation base.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="e852ef73-5251-41ca-a2a3-b6e45c5e4f33">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally and also decrease the account value, which in turn lowers the amount subjected to the 0.90% annual mortality &amp; expense risk charge, making the fee less impactful over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences cost</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="af4449ec-8861-4771-a54e-e9486c4a72d4">
      <data key="d3">Since the cost of insurance depends on the face amount at risk, any decrease from partial withdrawals reduces future COI charges under the stated formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="522644d7-e290-4908-b13c-663896d15b1c">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Face Amount at Risk from partial withdrawals results from lowering the Death Benefit, consistent with the definition provided in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reducing the face amount proportionally impact the effective exposure to sub-account expense ratios, since smaller balances still incur full expense ratios, increasing the relative cost burden on remaining capital.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies exposure</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.78</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="b927f377-e08d-4d88-b802-d2f9a5ecbad6">
      <data key="d3">Reduced face amounts from partial withdrawals alter asset allocation dynamics and could shift relative weightings in sub-accounts, potentially changing the average effective expense ratio experienced by investors.</data>
      <data key="d4">modulated by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d4b0a171-5ef3-4669-b3a4-2f4f8afafc3d" target="db0522da-0d9d-479f-9d33-41c3c624b1ce">
      <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reduce the face amount proportionally, which indirectly influences surrender charge calculations by lowering the policy's overall value base, thereby affecting the magnitude of any applicable surrender fees upon termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
