    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="e2d6b134-e378-4016-9aec-83160141d68a">
      <data key="d3">When a policy’s account value fails to meet monthly deductions for 61 consecutive days, triggering a lapse, a formal notice is required to be delivered at least 30 days beforehand to inform the policyholder.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="7f729579-af9d-4934-af44-77d11dd937c9">
      <data key="d3">The failure to maintain sufficient account value leads to policy lapse, creating the scenario under which reinstatement becomes necessary. Reinstatement eligibility within three years requires demonstrating continued insurability, making this a direct consequence of the lapse event.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="e381b39e-f494-4cde-959e-aff5ec7c393c">
      <data key="d3">The failure to maintain sufficient account value for 61 consecutive days triggers policy lapse, necessitating full repayment of missed payments plus 6% interest to reinstate coverage within three years.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes requiring</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="a270d4dd-8dc4-4636-bdb4-68ecbe2ee923">
      <data key="d3">The policy lapses if account value fails to meet deduction needs for 61 consecutive days, creating the scenario under which reinstatement becomes relevant. Repaying outstanding loans is required to restore coverage post-lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="bc4a44ad-5ecb-4ffc-b4fd-fdcc6934df7f">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s potential lapse due to insufficient funds is governed by rules applicable to its nature as a securities product subject to SEC regulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual relation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="5465f672-6731-400f-8a50-924b920bc0bf">
      <data key="d3">A policy lapse occurs when the account value cannot cover monthly deductions—such as the $15 administrative charge—for 61 consecutive days, making the charge a key factor in determining lapse eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="9038831d-df01-4459-b72d-e7af64e0f57a">
      <data key="d3">A policy lapse occurs when account value fails to sustain monthly deductions; since sub-account expense ratios erode account balance, they play a role in creating conditions that may trigger such a lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines the specific duration required for a lapse—61 consecutive days—which operationalizes the broader condition mentioned in fact_sentence_1 regarding insufficient account value.</data>
      <data key="d4">specifies threshold</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
