    <edge source="e2d6b134-e378-4016-9aec-83160141d68a" target="7f729579-af9d-4934-af44-77d11dd937c9">
      <data key="d3">The 30-day lapse notice ensures sufficient time for the policyholder to address issues before cancellation, allowing them to meet conditions like proving insurability required for reinstatement within three years.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e2d6b134-e378-4016-9aec-83160141d68a" target="e381b39e-f494-4cde-959e-aff5ec7c393c">
      <data key="d3">The 30-day lapse notice provides sufficient lead time for the policyholder to gather resources needed to satisfy reinstatement obligations, including payment of past due amounts and 6% interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e2d6b134-e378-4016-9aec-83160141d68a" target="a270d4dd-8dc4-4636-bdb4-68ecbe2ee923">
      <data key="d3">The 30-day lapse notice ensures the policyholder has time to act; if they wish to reinstate the policy within three years, repaying outstanding loans becomes necessary.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e2d6b134-e378-4016-9aec-83160141d68a" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for a 30-day lapse notice ensures policyholders have sufficient warning before their coverage terminates due to insufficient funds, aligning with the conditions under which a policy may lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
