    <edge source="e381b39e-f494-4cde-959e-aff5ec7c393c" target="de961a5e-5f41-4f5c-bf49-5a1e1747afb2">
      <data key="d3">To reinstate a lapsed policy within three years, one must repay overdue charges plus 6% interest, which applies only if the lapse was due to insufficient account value over 61 consecutive days.</data>
      <data key="d4">requires payment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e381b39e-f494-4cde-959e-aff5ec7c393c" target="e2d6b134-e378-4016-9aec-83160141d68a">
      <data key="d3">Meeting the reinstatement condition—paying back charges and 6% interest—is contingent on receiving timely notice; without the 30-day alert, compliance would not be feasible.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e381b39e-f494-4cde-959e-aff5ec7c393c" target="7f729579-af9d-4934-af44-77d11dd937c9">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the financial burden of reinstatement, requiring payment of past dues and 6% interest. This obligation supports fact_sentence_1’s requirement for proof of insurability by ensuring the policyholder meets economic responsibilities prior to reactivation.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e381b39e-f494-4cde-959e-aff5ec7c393c" target="a270d4dd-8dc4-4636-bdb4-68ecbe2ee923">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that reinstatement requires paying past due charges and 6% interest; this complements fact_sentence_2, which specifies repayment of outstanding loans as another necessary condition.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e381b39e-f494-4cde-959e-aff5ec7c393c" target="82754332-e72e-42c2-8178-8d00ac6d8b55">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay back charges plus 6% interest applies precisely when a policy has lapsed because the account value failed to meet deduction requirements, linking the two facts causally.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
